EXAM_DATA.papers["2006"] = {"id":"2006","year":2006,"label":"2006 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2006/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"The homeless make up a growing percentage of America's population.   {{1}}   , homelessness has reached such proportions that local governments can't possibly   {{2}}   . To help homeless people   {{3}}   independence, the federal government must support job training programs,   {{4}}   the minimum wage, and fund more low-cost housing."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"{{5}}   everyone agrees on the number of Americans who are homeless. Estimates   {{6}}   anywhere from 600,000 to 3 million.   {{7}}   the figure may vary, analysts do agree on another matter: that the number of the homeless is   {{8}}   . One of the federal government's studies   {{9}}   that the number of the homeless will reach nearly 19 million by the end of this decade."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"Finding ways to   {{10}}   this growing homeless population has become increasingly difficult.   {{11}}   when homeless individuals manage to find a   {{12}}   that will give them three meals a day and a place to sleep at night, a good number still spend the bulk of each day   {{13}}   the street. Part of the problem is that many homeless adults are addicted to alcohol or drugs. And a significant number of the homeless have serious mental disorders. Many others,   {{14}}   not addicted or mentally ill, simply lack the everyday   {{15}}   skills needed to turn their lives   {{16}}   . Boston Globe reporter Chris Reidy notes that the situation will improve only when there are   {{17}}   programs that address the many needs of the homeless.   {{18}}   Edward Zlotkowski, director of community service at Bentley College in Massachusetts,   {{19}}   it, \"There has to be   {{20}}   of programs. What's needed is a package deal.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Indeed"},{"key":"B","text":"Likewise"},{"key":"C","text":"Therefore"},{"key":"D","text":"Furthermore"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"1.","reason":"前后两句方向一致、后句是对前句的强调性升级 The homeless make up a growing percentage of America's population 给出事实，紧随的 homelessness has reached such proportions that local governments can't possibly __(2)__ 把同一事实推到「严重到地方政府无法应对」。这是「确实如此，而且程度严重」的语义，对应「强调＋确认」型连接。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Indeed 意为「确实，事实上」，常用于「前句说 X，紧接着把 X 强调到更深一层」的场合，正好对应这里「人数在涨——确实，已严峻到政府都顶不住了」的递进强调。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Likewise 用于两件并列、可类比的事情之间（如「A 也这样，B 也这样」）。原文前后句谈的是同一件事的同一面，谈不上类比，不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Therefore 要求前句是因、后句是果。「比例在上升」并不必然「严重到地方政府无力应对」——后者是程度判断，不是逻辑结论，因果关系不成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Furthermore 用于「除此之外还有另一点」，引出另一条信息。本句仍在说同一件事的同一个维度，没有新增信息点，且 Furthermore 缺少 Indeed 那层「确认强调」的语义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stand"},{"key":"B","text":"cope"},{"key":"C","text":"approve"},{"key":"D","text":"retain"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"本句线索＋下句「联邦必须出手」的因果暗示 本句 homelessness has reached such proportions that local governments can't possibly __(2)__ 在说地方政府「招架不住」，紧接着 the federal government must support job training programs 进一步说「所以联邦必须接手」。可见空处要表达「应付/处理（这种局面）」之意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"stand 表示「忍受」时常说 can't stand the noise/pain，与「应付一个公共问题」不搭；且 stand 表「应对」需 stand up to，单独用不达意。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"cope 的语义就是「成功地应对困难局面」（cope with a problem），与本句「问题严峻到政府无法应付」完美对接；尽管这里省略了 with（后接 with the problem 隐去），cope 作不及物动词独用表「应付得来」是地道用法。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"approve 与「政府是否赞成」毫无关系——政府要面对的是是否「处理得了」，不是是否「赞成」无家可归现象，语义不对。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"retain 表示「保留人员/职位/水分」，宾语是「想留住的东西」，但本句的潜在宾语是「严峻局面」，没有人想「保留」它，语义不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in"},{"key":"B","text":"for"},{"key":"C","text":"with"},{"key":"D","text":"toward"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"3.","reason":"动作语义是「帮助走向独立」、含方向性 To help homeless people __(3)__ independence 表达的是「帮无家可归者朝独立的方向迈进」——是一个动态过程，不是已经处在独立状态，也不是和独立同时进行。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"in 表 in independence「处于独立状态」是静态描述，但本句是动态过程「帮他们走向独立」，方向感缺失，不选。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"for 用 help sb for sth 不构成固定短语；help sb 后的动作通常用 to do 或介词 with/toward，for 表「为了」时句法应是 help for sth，与原句不合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"with 在 help sb with sth 中表示「协助处理某项具体事务」（如 help me with my homework），但 independence「独立」是一个状态目标，而非一件待处理的事，with 不达「迈向目标」之意，且语境上 toward 远更精准。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"toward 的核心义就是「朝……方向」，help sb toward independence 是英文报刊中的成熟表达，恰好对应「帮助无家可归者一步步走向独立」的动态过程。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"raise"},{"key":"B","text":"add"},{"key":"C","text":"take"},{"key":"D","text":"keep"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"并列项的方向一致性＋全段「帮助无家可归者」立场 并列其他两项 support job training programs（支持职业培训）和 fund more low-cost housing（资助更多低价房）都是「政府增加投入帮人」，方向都是「增加/提升」。同向并列下，空处必然也是「提升最低工资」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"raise 与 support job training programs、fund more low-cost housing 同为「政府正向投入」，raise the minimum wage 是英语财经新闻里几乎固定的搭配，正中题意。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"add 表「增加」时句法是 add sth to sth，单独 add the minimum wage 不成立；即便理解为「加薪」，英语里也说 raise/increase，不说 add a wage。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"take 与 wage 连用一般是 take a wage cut（接受降薪）或 take home a wage（拿回家工资），都不是「政府提高工资」的语义；且 take 与正向「帮无家可归者」立场反向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"keep 表「维持现状」，与并列两项的「新增投入」方向不一致；维持低工资恰恰无法改善无家可归者处境，立场反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Generally"},{"key":"B","text":"Almost"},{"key":"C","text":"Hardly"},{"key":"D","text":"Not"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"紧跟其后的数据范围给出「并非人人同意」的证据 下一句 Estimates __(6)__ anywhere from 600,000 to 3 million——估计数从 60 万到 300 万跨度极大，明显「人人意见不一」。空处只能填入表「并非人人」的部分否定词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Generally 是肯定语气「一般来说」，与下文 from 600,000 to 3 million 的明显分歧矛盾。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Almost 仍是肯定基调「几乎所有人」，同样与下文分歧的事实冲突，不选。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Hardly everyone agrees＝「几乎没人同意」程度过强；下文 analysts do agree on another matter（在另一件事上确有共识）显示并非「几乎没人同意任何事」，只是「不是所有人都同意人数」，Hardly 程度过头。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Not everyone 在英语里是固定的部分否定结构，表「不是所有人都……」，承认有人同意有人不同意，与下文「估计数从 60 万到 300 万」的分歧及后文「在另一点上确有共识」都吻合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cover"},{"key":"B","text":"change"},{"key":"C","text":"range"},{"key":"D","text":"differ"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"from… to… 数字跨度结构本身即线索 anywhere from 600,000 to 3 million 明白表示「跨度从 60 万到 300 万」，搭配动词 range，构成 range from… to…「在……到……之间变动」的固定结构。本句即可定答案，无需跨句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"cover 表「涵盖、覆盖」时通常直接接宾语（cover the topic / cover 50 miles），不与 anywhere from X to Y 形成固定搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"change 强调「前后状态不同」，但 Estimates 是多家估计同时存在的并列数字，并非同一估计在变。change from X to Y 表「由 X 变成 Y」，不对应 anywhere 多点跨度。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"range 与 from X to Y 构成 range from… to…「在 X 到 Y 之间变动」的固定搭配，且常与 anywhere 连用强调跨度之广，完全对应 Estimates __(6)__ anywhere from 600,000 to 3 million。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"differ 的固定搭配是 differ from「与…不同」，不与 from… to… 同时搭配；且 differ 只表「不同」、没有「在区间内分布」的意味。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Now that"},{"key":"B","text":"Although"},{"key":"C","text":"Provided"},{"key":"D","text":"Except that"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"7.","reason":"前句「数字可能不同」 vs 后句「在另一件事上确有共识」 前分句 the figure may vary 承认数据不一致，后分句 analysts do agree on another matter 转而强调专家在另一点上有共识。前否后肯，是典型让步关系。注意后句的 do agree 用助动词 do 强调，再次确认这是让步＋强调结构。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Now that 引出原因「既然 X，所以 Y」，但「数字不一」并不是「专家在另一件事上有共识」的原因，因果链不成立。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Although 的「虽然 X，但还是 Y」结构与 the figure may vary、analysts do agree on another matter 严丝合缝，后句 do agree 的强调也呼应让步语气。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Provided 引导条件状语，表示「假如 X，则 Y」；但 the figure may vary 是已经存在的事实，不是待满足的条件，逻辑不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Except that 用法是「X，except that Y」，Y 是对 X 的唯一限制；但本句是先说「数字不一」、再说「但在另一点上一致」，两件事是让步对比，不是「X 都对，只有 Y 不一样」的例外限制。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"inflating"},{"key":"B","text":"expanding"},{"key":"C","text":"increasing"},{"key":"D","text":"extending"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"主语是 the number，下句给出具体上升数据 本句 the number of the homeless is __(8)__ 与下句 the number of the homeless will reach nearly 19 million by the end of this decade 共同描绘「人数将不断上升」。主语 the number 与「数字增长」连用，英语最标准的动词就是 increase。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"inflating 多用于气球膨胀、物价上涨（inflation 通货膨胀），与「无家可归者人数」搭配不地道，也带「虚高、不真实」的贬义色彩，与本句客观陈述不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"expanding 强调「向外扩张」（市场扩张、业务扩张、宇宙膨胀），主语是可在空间上扩展的事物；the number 是一个抽象计数，不在空间上扩张，搭配不当。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"increasing 与主语 the number 是教科书级搭配 The number is increasing，且与下句 will reach nearly 19 million 的预测完全自洽，是唯一的最优解。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"extending 用于 extend a deadline / extend a road / extend the area，强调长度或范围的延伸，无法形容「数量本身的增加」。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"predicts"},{"key":"B","text":"displays"},{"key":"C","text":"proves"},{"key":"D","text":"discovers"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"that 从句的 will reach 是将来时，指向「预测」 the number of the homeless will reach nearly 19 million by the end of this decade 是一个尚未发生的未来数字，表预测；与「研究」搭配，标准动词就是 predict。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"predicts 专表「对未来作预测」，主语可以是 study/report/expert/model，宾语 that 从句多用将来时——与 will reach nearly 19 million by the end of this decade 的将来时预测完全匹配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"displays 用于 display a chart/painting/talent，宾语是看得见的东西；与「研究 + that 从句」搭配不地道，也无法承载「预测」之意。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"proves 表「以证据证明」，宾语从句须是可被证据证实的事实（多为现在/过去时）。但 will reach nearly 19 million by the end of this decade 是尚未发生的预测，无法被「证明」，逻辑矛盾。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"discovers 强调「找出原本就存在但未被知晓的事实」，宾语是已存在的真相，不能用来「发现一个尚未发生的未来数字」。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"assist"},{"key":"B","text":"track"},{"key":"C","text":"sustain"},{"key":"D","text":"dismiss"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"段首主张＋全段对策语境 段1已立 To help homeless people __(3)__ independence，本段开头 Finding ways to __(10)__ this growing homeless population has become increasingly difficult 紧承「帮人之难」展开，下文又列举原因（成瘾、精神障碍、缺技能）解释为何「帮起来难」。空处必填「帮助」之意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"assist 是 help 的近义书面词，宾语是被帮的对象（assist the elderly / assist this population），与全段「找方法帮无家可归者」的语境完美吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"track 是「追踪、追查」（追踪嫌犯、追踪数据），与「帮助这群人」无关，且全段不在讨论统计数据，立场偏离。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"sustain 表「维持现状」，sustain this population＝「让这个群体继续保持现在的状态」，与「帮他们摆脱困境」立场冲突；且 sustain 多与 effort/growth/life 等抽象名词搭配，不与「人群」直接搭配表帮助。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"dismiss 表「忽视、驳回、解雇」，dismiss the homeless 是冷漠态度，与作者呼吁帮助的立场南辕北辙。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Hence"},{"key":"B","text":"But"},{"key":"C","text":"Even"},{"key":"D","text":"Only"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"主句 still 是让步加强的明显标志 主句 a good number still spend the bulk of each day __(13)__ the street 中 still 明确表示「仍然」，对应 when 从句 homeless individuals manage to find a __(12)__「即便他们找到了庇护」。Even + when + 主句 still 是典型「即便……仍然……」结构。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Hence 引出结果，但「找到庇护」并不导致「仍流落街头」，因果链不通；且 Hence when 的搭配不地道。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"But 一般用于连接两个分句开头（句首 But, …），不接 when 引导的从句作 But when。句法上不顺、也与 still 形成赘余。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Even 与 when 构成 Even when「即使在……时候」让步状语，与主句 a good number still spend the bulk of each day 的 still 完美呼应，是英语让步加强的典型结构。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Only 与 when 构成 Only when…「只有当……才」，主句要倒装（Only when… do they…），且语义是「仅在某条件下才发生」，与本句「即便有庇护仍流浪街头」完全相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lodging"},{"key":"B","text":"shelter"},{"key":"C","text":"dwelling"},{"key":"D","text":"house"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"「提供一日三餐＋夜间睡处」的描述指向救助所 that will give them three meals a day and a place to sleep at night 描述的是免费／救助性质的食宿，正是英语 shelter（特别是 homeless shelter）的标准定义。这是英语社会语境的固定搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"lodging 是旅行或短期外出时的住宿（如 board and lodging），通常需付费，与「免费救助流浪者并提供三餐」的语境不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"shelter 在英语社会语境里就是为流浪者、灾民、受家暴者提供免费食宿与保护的救助场所（homeless shelter），与 three meals a day and a place to sleep at night 的描述完全对应。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"dwelling 是法律/统计语境用词，指任何「人类居住的单位」，没有「救助、提供食宿」的语义色彩，且过于正式，与本句不搭。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"house 是一个家庭住宅或独立房屋，是「家」的概念；无家可归者「找到了一个 house」反而矛盾——他们正缺 house，且 house 不提供集体食宿。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"searching"},{"key":"B","text":"strolling"},{"key":"C","text":"crowding"},{"key":"D","text":"wandering"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"主语「无家可归者」＋「白天大半时间」共同指向「无目的地游荡」 a good number still spend the bulk of each day __(13)__ the street 主语是「相当多的无家可归者」，方式状语是「整日大半时间」——这群人既无固定工作也无目的地，整日在街上「漫无目的地游荡」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"searching 通常带宾语（searching for food / searching the street for sb），表「为找特定目标」搜寻；本句无明确目标，且 searching the street 也不构成「无目的游荡」之意。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"strolling 暗含「悠闲、惬意」的休闲意味（饭后漫步、公园散步），与无家可归者整日流落街头的窘迫处境色彩冲突，且 stroll 多与 in/along 搭配。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"crowding 表「拥挤在某处」，主语通常是大批人群同时涌入一地（crowding the square），但本句是「相当多的人各自消磨时间」、不是「同时涌挤一处」，语义不对。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"wandering 的核心义是「漫无目的地走来走去」，且常用于流浪者/迷失者的语境（wander the streets 是英语外刊高频搭配），完美对接本句的主语身份与「整日消磨」的状态。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"when"},{"key":"B","text":"once"},{"key":"C","text":"while"},{"key":"D","text":"whereas"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"14.","reason":"前句提到「成瘾/精神病」是难题、本句说另一类人「不是这两种但仍有别的难题」 上一句 many homeless adults are addicted to alcohol or drugs. And a significant number of the homeless have serious mental disorders 列出两种原因，本句 Many others, __(14)__ not addicted or mentally ill, simply lack the everyday __(15)__ skills 转到另一类人，让步地说「他们虽不是这两类，但仍缺乏生存技能」。这是「虽然……但是……」的让步对比。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"when 引导时间状语，但本句不是「在他们不成瘾时缺技能」的时间限定，而是「即使不成瘾也缺技能」的让步对比，方向不对。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"once 含「一旦……就」的条件起点意味，但本句不在描述「一旦不成瘾就缺技能」的触发条件，与原意不合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"while 引导让步状语「虽然不成瘾、也不精神病，但仍缺日常生存技能」，是英语作品中表让步＋对比的高频用法，尤其在 Subject, while X, still Y 结构中最自然。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"whereas 是较为正式的对比连词，常用于 X, whereas Y 形式连两个完整分句，不太用作主语后的插入状语开头，且原句这里更偏让步而非纯并列对比，让步更准。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"life"},{"key":"B","text":"existence"},{"key":"C","text":"survival"},{"key":"D","text":"maintenance"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"「靠这种 skills 翻身」的目标语境指向「生存技能」 simply lack the everyday __(15)__ skills needed to turn their lives __(16)__——这是「翻转生活、走出困境」所需的技能，且无家可归者面临的是「能否在艰难处境下活下去并自立」，正是 survival skills 「生存技能」的语义场。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"life skills 在英语里确指「日常生活技能」（理财、烹饪、社交等），是颇有干扰性的近义干扰项；但与「无家可归者翻身」语境对比，survival 比 life 更贴合「在艰难处境下自立生存」的语义场，且文中已用 everyday，再用 life 语义重复，反不如 survival 锐利。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"existence 「存在/生存」是抽象哲学用词，无 existence skills 这一固定搭配，英语里不这么说。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"survival skills 是英语成熟搭配，专指「在艰难处境下活下去并自立的技能」（野外、灾区、贫困都用），与无家可归者「缺少这一技能就无法 turn their lives around」的处境完全对应。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"maintenance skills 在英语里指「维修保养技能」（车辆、设备），是机械维护语境，与无家可归者的人生困境完全不搭。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"around"},{"key":"B","text":"over"},{"key":"C","text":"on"},{"key":"D","text":"up"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"16.","reason":"上下文表达「让人生彻底好转」的语境 simply lack the everyday __(15)__ skills needed to turn their lives __(16)__——他们缺技能、人生陷困境，所需要的正是「彻底扭转人生」的技能。turn one's life around 在英语里就是「彻底扭转人生、走出困境」的固定说法。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"around 与 turn 构成 turn one's life around「让人生彻底好转」（也可 turn a company around=让公司起死回生），是英语固定的「逆转、扭转」短语，与本句意旨完全对应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"over 与 turn 构成 turn over 表「翻转过来」或「移交（财物/权力）」（turn over the keys），与「扭转人生」语义不合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"on 与 turn 构成 turn on，表「打开电源」或「（人）突然攻击」（turn on sb），不能用于 turn one's life on。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"up 与 turn 构成 turn up，常见义是「出现」或「调高音量」，turn one's life up 不是英语固定说法，语义也不指向「扭转」。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"complex"},{"key":"B","text":"comprehensive"},{"key":"C","text":"complementary"},{"key":"D","text":"compensating"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"「address the many needs」 + 后文「package deal」均指向「综合性/全方位」 本句 address the many needs of the homeless（解决多重需求）已是强信号；下句更明确 There has to be __(20)__ of programs. What's needed is a package deal（需要一揽子方案）。两处都指向「项目要全面、综合」，对应 comprehensive。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"complex 强调「复杂、错综」，可能含贬义（complex but useless），与「全面解决多种需求」的「综合」之意不同；项目要「综合全面」不一定要「复杂难懂」。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"comprehensive 强调「覆盖所有方面、综合全面」（comprehensive plan, comprehensive insurance），正是「能同时回应多重需求」的项目所需特质，与下文 a package deal 严丝合缝。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"complementary 强调两者之间「互补」（complementary colors），需要前后并置；单独说 complementary programs 不构成「全面」之意，与原意不合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"compensating 强调「弥补、补偿」（compensating payment），与「项目要全面涵盖多种需求」无对应；本句不在讨论补偿，立场偏离。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"So"},{"key":"B","text":"Since"},{"key":"C","text":"As"},{"key":"D","text":"Thus"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"18.","reason":"puts it 自身即铁证，定 as __(18)__ Edward Zlotkowski, director of community service at Bentley College in Massachusetts, __(19)__ it, \"There has to be __(20)__ of programs.\"——这是直接引用 Zlotkowski 的原话，标准句式为 as sb puts it 「正如某人所说」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"So 是因果连词，不与 puts it 搭配；So Edward puts it 不是英语句式，且语义上前后句也无因果。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Since 是因果/时间连词，与 puts it 不搭配，且语义上也不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"As 与 puts it 构成 as sb puts it「正如某人所说」，是引出原话的成熟句式，与紧随其后的直接引语 \"There has to be __(20)__ of programs.\" 完全对应。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Thus 是结论性副词「因此」，与 puts it 不构成固定句式；语义上也不指向「引述」。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"puts"},{"key":"B","text":"interprets"},{"key":"C","text":"assumes"},{"key":"D","text":"makes"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"19.","reason":"as sb puts it 中 puts 是不可替换的核心动词 __(18)__ Edward Zlotkowski, director of community service at Bentley College in Massachusetts, __(19)__ it, \"There has to be __(20)__ of programs.\"——本空与 18 题的 as 联手构成 as sb puts it 固定引述框架，其中 puts 是不可替换的核心动词，意为「（用某种方式）表达、说」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"puts 与 it 构成 puts it「（这样）说道」，与 as 联动构成 as sb puts it 引述结构；后接直接引语 \"There has to be __(20)__ of programs.\" 自然成立。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"interprets 多带具体宾语（interpret the data），表「解读」；as sb interprets it 不是英语固定的引人话结构。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"assumes 表「假定、设想」，主语在做尚未证实的推测；本句是引用 Zlotkowski 已说出口的具体观点，不是假设。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"makes 与 it 构成 make it 表「成功/到达/赶上」（made it to the top），与「（用某种方式）说出」无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"supervision"},{"key":"B","text":"manipulation"},{"key":"C","text":"regulation"},{"key":"D","text":"coordination"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"package deal 是空处的同义复述，锁定 coordination There has to be __(20)__ of programs. What's needed is a package deal——两句构成同义复述，package deal「一揽子方案」的语义核心是「多项程序作为整体协调推进」，正对 coordination of programs「项目间的协调」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"supervision 强调「上对下的监督」，supervision of programs 偏「对项目进行督查」，与 package deal「多项目协同打包」不对应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"manipulation 在英语中常带负面色彩「操控、暗箱操作」，与作者「呼吁综合方案」的正向立场冲突。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"regulation 强调「立法/规章约束」，regulation of programs 偏「对项目的规范管理」，仍不是 package deal 所要求的「各项目联动配合」。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"coordination 「协调、协同」是 package deal 的核心机制——多个项目作为一个整体彼此配合，与 What's needed is a package deal 严丝合缝，也与全文「综合施策」立场一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"In spite of \"endless talk of difference,\" American society is an amazing machine for homogenizing people. There is \"the democratizing uniformity of dress and discourse, and the casualness and absence of deference\" characteristic of popular culture. People are absorbed into \"a culture of consumption\" launched by the 19th-century department stores that offered \"vast arrays of goods in an elegant atmosphere. Instead of intimate shops catering to a knowledgeable elite,\" these were stores \"anyone could enter, regardless of class or background. This turned shopping into a public and democratic act.\" The mass media, advertising and sports are other forces for homogenization."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Immigrants are quickly fitting into this common culture, which may not be altogether elevating but is hardly poisonous. Writing for the National Immigration Forum, Gregory Rodriguez reports that today's immigration is neither at unprecedented levels nor resistant to assimilation. In 1998 immigrants were 9.8 percent of the population; in 1900, 13.6 percent. In the 10 years prior to 1990, 3.1 immigrants arrived for every 1,000 residents; in the 10 years prior to 1890, 9.2 for every 1,000. Now, consider three indices of assimilation – language, home ownership and intermarriage."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"The 1990 Census revealed that \"a majority of immigrants from each of the fifteen most common countries of origin spoke English 'well' or 'very well' after ten years of residence.\" The children of immigrants tend to be bilingual and proficient in English. \"By the third generation, the original language is lost in the majority of immigrant families.\" Hence the description of America as a \"graveyard\" for languages. By 1996 foreign-born immigrants who had arrived before 1970 had a home ownership rate of 75.6 percent, higher than the 69.8 percent rate among native-born Americans."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Foreign-born Asians and Hispanics \"have higher rates of intermarriage than do U.S.-born whites and blacks.\" By the third generation, one third of Hispanic women are married to non-Hispanics, and 41 percent of Asian-American women are married to non-Asians."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"Rodriguez notes that children in remote villages around the world are fans of superstars like Arnold Schwarzenegger and Garth Brooks, yet \"some Americans fear that immigrants living within the United States remain somehow immune to the nation's assimilative power.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"Are there divisive issues and pockets of seething anger in America? Indeed. It is big enough to have a bit of everything. But particularly when viewed against America's turbulent past, today's social indices hardly suggest a dark and deteriorating social environment."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"The word \"homogenizing\" (Line 2, Paragraph 1) most probably means____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"identifying."},{"key":"B","text":"associating."},{"key":"C","text":"assimilating."},{"key":"D","text":"monopolizing."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"第1段第2行中的\"homogenizing\"一词最可能的意思是____","choicesZh":{"A":"识别","B":"联合","C":"同化","D":"垄断"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"homogenizing\" (Line 2, Paragraph 1) most probably means 直接给出词、位置和「最可能意思是」，是词义题的标准模板。","parse":"Q21 主干是 The word ... most probably means ____，括号里 Line 2, Paragraph 1 是位置状语；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"American society is an amazing machine for homogenizing people. There is \"the democratizing uniformity of dress and discourse, and the casualness and absence of deference\" characteristic of popular culture.","locateZh":"美国社会是一台令人惊叹的「同化」人的机器。流行文化具有「服饰与言谈的民主化划一、随意感以及恭敬的缺席」的特征。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"identify 常考义为「辨认、确认身份」，没有「使……合为一体」的语义；这是利用 identify 与 identical（相同的）形近来诱导考生，但二者动作方向完全不同。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"associate 表「把 A 与 B 联系起来」，强调建立关联而非合并差异；原文说美国是把人「磨平差异」的机器，与「建立联系」方向不同。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"把预判的「使融为一体」拿去比对四项，只有 assimilating 与「uniformity / fitting into common culture」语义一致，直接锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"the democratizing uniformity of dress and discourse","opt":"assimilating"},{"orig":"Immigrants are quickly fitting into this common culture","opt":"assimilating"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"monopolize 的对象通常是市场、资源、话语权，而不是「人」；它带强烈的「独占」色彩，与原文「democratizing uniformity」的「民主化」基调正相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"According to the author, the department stores of the 19th century____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"played a role in the spread of popular culture."},{"key":"B","text":"became intimate shops for common consumers."},{"key":"C","text":"satisfied the needs of a knowledgeable elite."},{"key":"D","text":"owed its emergence to the culture of consumption."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,19世纪的百货商店____","choicesZh":{"A":"在大众文化的传播中发挥了作用","B":"成为普通消费者的私密商店","C":"满足了知识精英的需求","D":"其出现归功于消费文化"},"analysis":{"type":"According to the author, the department stores of the 19th century 指向一个具体客观事实，回原文能找到对应陈述，是典型细节题。","parse":"Q22 是不完整陈述句，选项是 the department stores of the 19th century 的谓语延续；考生须把题干 + 选项当一整句读，避免只读题干就匹配关键词。","locateEn":"People are absorbed into \"a culture of consumption\" launched by the 19th-century department stores that offered \"vast arrays of goods in an elegant atmosphere.\" ... This turned shopping into a public and democratic act. The mass media, advertising and sports are other forces for homogenization.","locateZh":"人们被吸纳进由 19 世纪百货商店所开启的「消费文化」之中，这些商店在优雅的氛围里提供大量商品……这使购物变成了一种公共且民主的行为。大众媒体、广告与体育是其他的同化力量。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判中的「推动 + 消费/流行文化」与 played a role in the spread of popular culture. 在动作（推动）与对象（流行文化）上都对得上，唯一答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"a \"culture of consumption\" launched by the 19th-century department stores","opt":"played a role in the spread of popular culture."},{"orig":"a culture of consumption","opt":"popular culture"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Instead of intimate shops catering to a knowledgeable elite, these were stores anyone could enter 明确说百货商店「不是 intimate shops」、而是任何人都能进的店；选项却说百货商店「成了 intimate shops」，方向完全颠倒。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说百货商店与「intimate shops catering to a knowledgeable elite」相对立，anyone could enter, regardless of class or background；选项却说商店「满足了见多识广的精英的需要」，与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 a \"culture of consumption\" launched by the 19th-century department stores 中 launched by 表明：消费文化是被百货商店开启的——商店是因，文化是果。选项却说百货商店「应归功于消费文化」，把因果整个翻转。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The text suggests that immigrants now in the U.S. ____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"are resistant to homogenization."},{"key":"B","text":"exert a great influence on American culture."},{"key":"C","text":"are hardly a threat to the common culture."},{"key":"D","text":"constitute the majority of the population."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"文章表明现在美国的移民____","choicesZh":{"A":"抵制同化","B":"对美国文化产生巨大影响","C":"几乎不对共同文化构成威胁","D":"构成人口的大多数"},"analysis":{"type":"The text suggests that immigrants now in the U.S. 含 suggests，提示答案需在文本基础上做一步逻辑延伸。","parse":"Q23 主干 The text suggests that ...，that 引导宾语从句；选项是从句的谓语延续，整体结构清晰。","locateEn":"Immigrants are quickly fitting into this common culture, which may not be altogether elevating but is hardly poisonous. ... today's immigration is neither at unprecedented levels nor resistant to assimilation.","locateZh":"移民正快速融入这种共通文化——这种文化未必完全是「提升人格」的，但也几乎称不上「有毒」。……今天的移民既未达到前所未有的规模，也并非抗拒同化。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说移民「并非抗拒同化」，A 却说「抵抗同质化」，方向反着来。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文讲的是移民「融入」共通文化（被同化），而不是移民「影响」共通文化（去同化别人）；方向是单向被吸收，不是双向互塑。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"把预判中的「不构成威胁」拿去对四项，are hardly a threat to the common culture 同义复述，无歧义。","pairs":[{"orig":"is hardly poisonous","opt":"are hardly a threat to the common culture"},{"orig":"today's immigration is neither at unprecedented levels nor resistant to assimilation","opt":"are hardly a threat to the common culture"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 In 1998 immigrants were 9.8 percent of the population 明确移民只占人口 9.8%，远非「占多数」；D 把比例错读为「构成大多数」。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"Why are Arnold Schwarzenegger and Garth Brooks mentioned in Paragraph 5?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To prove their popularity around the world."},{"key":"B","text":"To reveal the public's fear of immigrants."},{"key":"C","text":"To give examples of successful immigrants."},{"key":"D","text":"To show the powerful influence of American culture."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"为什么在第5段中提到Arnold Schwarzenegger和Garth Brooks?","choicesZh":{"A":"为了证明他们在世界各地的受欢迎程度","B":"为了揭示公众对移民的恐惧","C":"为了举出成功移民的例子","D":"为了展示美国文化的强大影响力"},"analysis":{"type":"Why are Arnold Schwarzenegger and Garth Brooks mentioned in Paragraph 5? 直接问「为什么被提到」，是例证目的题的固定问法。","parse":"Q24 被动疑问句 Why are X mentioned in ...，重心在 Why；考生不要被人名本身分散注意力，问的是「为什么提」而不是「提了什么」。","locateEn":"Rodriguez notes that children in remote villages around the world are fans of superstars like Arnold Schwarzenegger and Garth Brooks, yet \"some Americans fear that immigrants living within the United States remain somehow immune to the nation's assimilative power.\"","locateZh":"Rodriguez 指出，世界各地偏远村庄的孩子都是阿诺·施瓦辛格、Garth Brooks 这类巨星的粉丝，然而「一些美国人却担心住在美国境内的移民不知怎的就对这个国家的同化力免疫」。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"「世界各地是粉丝」固然事实上证明了两位明星的流行，但作者举例的目的不是介绍这两位明星有多红，而是借这个事实推进自己关于「美国文化同化力」的论证。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文用 yet 把「some Americans fear ... immune to the nation's assimilative power」呈现为一种被反讽的担忧；作者本人并不认同这种担忧，更不是为了「揭示」它而举例。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"选项打的是「施瓦辛格本人是奥地利移民」这种考生背景常识擦边球；但原文从头到尾没提两位明星的移民身份，他们在文中只是「美国流行文化的代言人」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判结论与 To show the powerful influence of American culture. 完全同义，无须二想。","pairs":[{"orig":"children in remote villages around the world are fans of superstars like Arnold Schwarzenegger and Garth Brooks","opt":"To show the powerful influence of American culture."}]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"In the author's opinion, the absorption of immigrants into American society is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rewarding."},{"key":"B","text":"successful."},{"key":"C","text":"fruitless."},{"key":"D","text":"harmful."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"态度题","stemZh":"在作者看来,移民融入美国社会是____","choicesZh":{"A":"有益的","B":"成功的","C":"徒劳的","D":"有害的"},"analysis":{"type":"In the author's opinion, the absorption of immigrants into American society is 直接问作者对全文主话题的评价，选项全部为态度形容词。","parse":"Q25 是不完整陈述句，主语 the absorption of immigrants into American society 较长，is 之后由选项补完；考生须看清主语整体后再填态度词。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"rewarding 强调融入对移民个人「值得 / 有回报」，文章关心的是融入是否在发生、是否有害于美国社会，并未评价对移民个人的回报；属于错位评价。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项里 successful. 与预判「成功」一字对应，且能同时被首段主论、中段数据、末段总评三处共同支撑。","pairs":[{"orig":"Immigrants are quickly fitting into this common culture","opt":"successful."},{"orig":"today's social indices hardly suggest a dark and deteriorating social environment","opt":"successful."},{"orig":"By 1996 foreign-born immigrants who had arrived before 1970 had a home ownership rate of 75.6 percent, higher than the 69.8 percent rate among native-born Americans.","opt":"successful."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"fruitless 意为「没有成果的」，原文反复给出数据证明融入是有成果的（购房率、英语水平、通婚率），方向恰好相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 may not be altogether elevating but is hardly poisonous 已经明确说融入「几乎不有害」，D 却说「有害」，正反颠倒。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Stratford-on-Avon, as we all know, has only one industry – William Shakespeare – but there are two distinctly separate and increasingly hostile branches. There is the Royal Shakespeare Company (RSC), which presents superb productions of the plays at the Shakespeare Memorial Theatre on the Avon. And there are the townsfolk who largely live off the tourists who come, not to see the plays, but to look at Anne Hathaway's Cottage, Shakespeare's birthplace and the other sights."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"The worthy residents of Stratford doubt that the theater adds a penny to their revenue. They frankly dislike the RSC's actors, them with their long hair and beards and sandals and noisiness. It's all deliciously ironic when you consider that Shakespeare, who earns their living, was himself an actor (with a beard) and did his share of noise-making."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"The tourist streams are not entirely separate. The sightseers who come by bus – and often take in Warwick Castle and Blenheim Palace on the side – don't usually see the plays, and some of them are even surprised to find a theatre in Stratford. However, the playgoers do manage a little sight-seeing along with their playgoing. It is the playgoers, the RSC contends, who bring in much of the town's revenue because they spend the night (some of them four or five nights) pouring cash into the hotels and restaurants. The sightseers can take in everything and get out of town by nightfall."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"The townsfolk don't see it this way and the local council does not contribute directly to the subsidy of the Royal Shakespeare Company. Stratford cries poor traditionally. Nevertheless every hotel in town seems to be adding a new wing or cocktail lounge. Hilton is building its own hotel there, which you may be sure will be decorated with Hamlet Hamburger Bars, the Lear Lounge, the Banquo Banqueting Room, and so forth, and will be very expensive."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"Anyway, the townsfolk can't understand why the Royal Shakespeare Company needs a subsidy. (The theatre has broken attendance records for three years in a row. Last year its 1,431 seats were 94 per cent occupied all year long and this year they'll do better.) The reason, of course, is that costs have rocketed and ticket prices have stayed low."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"It would be a shame to raise prices too much because it would drive away the young people who are Stratford's most attractive clientele. They come entirely for the plays, not the sights. They all seem to look alike (though they come from all over) – lean, pointed, dedicated faces, wearing jeans and sandals, eating their buns and bedding down for the night on the flagstones outside the theatre to buy the 20 seats and 80 standing-room tickets held for the sleepers and sold to them when the box office opens at 10:30 a.m."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"From the first two paragraphs, we learn that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the townsfolk deny the RSC's contribution to the town's revenue."},{"key":"B","text":"the actors of the RSC imitate Shakespeare on and off stage."},{"key":"C","text":"the two branches of the RSC are not on good terms."},{"key":"D","text":"the townsfolk earn little from tourism."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从前两段我们可以得知____","choicesZh":{"A":"镇民否认RSC对该镇收入的贡献。","B":"RSC的演员在台上台下都模仿莎士比亚。","C":"RSC的两个分支关系不睦。","D":"镇民从旅游业中获利甚微。"},"analysis":{"type":"we learn that 后跟的是一个待补完的陈述句,要求选出与前两段事实最一致的一项,没有 infer/imply 之类的推断信号。","parse":"From the first two paragraphs, we learn that____ 是 \"From + 来源状语,we learn that + 宾语从句\" 的标准句式,选项接在 that 后充当宾语从句,结构平铺直叙,无陷阱。","locateEn":"The worthy residents of Stratford doubt that the theater adds a penny to their revenue.","locateZh":"斯特拉特福那些可敬的居民们怀疑剧院能给他们的收入多增加哪怕一便士。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判要点\"镇民不认 RSC 给镇带来收入\"与 the townsfolk deny the RSC's contribution to the town's revenue 完全同义,直接锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"The worthy residents of Stratford doubt that the theater adds a penny to their revenue","opt":"the townsfolk deny the RSC's contribution to the town's revenue"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"第 2 段只用反讽口吻指出莎士比亚本人也是长着胡子、爱吵闹的演员,从未说 RSC 演员在台上台下\"刻意模仿\"莎士比亚。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 two distinctly separate and increasingly hostile branches 指的是 RSC 与镇民这两派对立,而 the two branches of the RSC 把对立双方限定到了 RSC 内部,主语弄错了。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the townsfolk who largely live off the tourists 明确说镇民主要靠游客为生,即从旅游业赚的不少,而 the townsfolk earn little from tourism 说镇民从旅游业赚得少,与原文相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 3 that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the sightseers cannot visit the Castle and the Palace separately."},{"key":"B","text":"the playgoers spend more money than the sightseers."},{"key":"C","text":"the sightseers do more shopping than the playgoers."},{"key":"D","text":"the playgoers go to no other places in town than the theater."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第三段可以推断出____","choicesZh":{"A":"观光客无法分别参观城堡和宫殿。","B":"看戏的人比观光客花费更多。","C":"观光客比看戏的人购物更多。","D":"看戏的人在镇上除了剧院不去其他地方。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 3 that 中的 inferred 明确要求做推断,而非细节复述。","parse":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 3 that____ 是 It 形式主语 + 被动 can be inferred + from 状语 + that 真正主语从句,选项接在 that 后做主语从句,结构常规、无陷阱。","locateEn":"It is the playgoers, the RSC contends, who bring in much of the town's revenue because they spend the night (some of them four or five nights) pouring cash into the hotels and restaurants. The sightseers can take in everything and get out of town by nightfall.","locateZh":"RSC 主张,正是看戏的人带来了镇上大部分收入,因为他们要在镇上过夜(有些人甚至住四五晚),把现金大把地花在酒店和餐厅里。而观光客一天就能逛完,天黑前就出镇了。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 often take in Warwick Castle and Blenheim Palace on the side 只是说观光者会顺路同游,从未说他们不能分开去华威城堡和布伦海姆宫。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"看戏者花钱比观光者多\"与 the playgoers spend more money than the sightseers 完全对应,锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"they spend the night (some of them four or five nights) pouring cash into the hotels and restaurants","opt":"the playgoers spend more money than the sightseers"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说看戏者把钱花在 hotels and restaurants,只字未提观光者的购物;\"购物谁多\"在第 3 段根本没有可比对的事实。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 the playgoers do manage a little sight-seeing along with their playgoing 明确说看戏者会顺便观光、去过其他地方,选项却说\"除剧院外哪里都不去\",方向相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"By saying \"Stratford cries poor traditionally\" (Line 2, Paragraph 4), the author implies that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Stratford cannot afford the expansion projects."},{"key":"B","text":"Stratford has long been in financial difficulties."},{"key":"C","text":"the town is not really short of money."},{"key":"D","text":"the townsfolk used to be poorly paid."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"通过说\"Stratford历来哭穷\"(第四段第2行),作者暗示____","choicesZh":{"A":"Stratford负担不起扩建项目。","B":"Stratford长期以来一直处于财政困难之中。","C":"该镇并非真的缺钱。","D":"镇民过去收入微薄。"},"analysis":{"type":"By saying \"Stratford cries poor traditionally\" (Line 2, Paragraph 4), the author implies that 锁定的是这一具体句子的言外之意,是典型的句意题。","parse":"By saying \"Stratford cries poor traditionally\" (Line 2, Paragraph 4), the author implies that____ 主干是 \"the author implies that...\",前面的 By saying \"...\" 是介词短语作方式状语,(Line 2, Paragraph 4) 是插入语标位,选项做 that 宾语从句,结构清晰。","locateEn":"Stratford cries poor traditionally. Nevertheless every hotel in town seems to be adding a new wing or cocktail lounge. Hilton is building its own hotel there, which you may be sure will be decorated with Hamlet Hamburger Bars, the Lear Lounge, the Banquo Banqueting Room, and so forth, and will be very expensive.","locateZh":"斯特拉特福一向\"哭穷\"。然而镇上几乎每家酒店都在加建新翼或鸡尾酒廊;希尔顿还在那里新建自己的酒店,可以肯定它会被装点成\"哈姆雷特汉堡吧\"、\"李尔酒廊\"、\"班戈宴会厅\"等等,而且会非常昂贵。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文恰恰说镇上有大把扩建工程(every hotel in town seems to be adding a new wing or cocktail lounge),没有任何\"承担不起\"的信号。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Stratford has long been in financial difficulties 把引语 Stratford cries poor traditionally 按字面直译过来,完全无视紧随其后的 Nevertheless 揭穿,正是作者要反讽的对象。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"嘴上哭穷其实不穷\"与 the town is not really short of money 形式一致(否定 + really),直接锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"Nevertheless every hotel in town seems to be adding a new wing or cocktail lounge","opt":"the town is not really short of money"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the townsfolk used to be poorly paid 把话题从\"镇财政\"偷换为\"镇民工资\",还把现在的\"哭穷\"改成过去时\"曾经工资低\",对象和时态双重错位。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"According to the townsfolk, the RSC deserves no subsidy because____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ticket prices can be raised to cover the spending."},{"key":"B","text":"the company is financially ill-managed."},{"key":"C","text":"the behavior of the actors is not socially acceptable."},{"key":"D","text":"the theatre attendance is on the rise."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据镇民的看法,RSC不应获得补贴,因为____","choicesZh":{"A":"可以提高票价来支付开支。","B":"该剧团财务管理不善。","C":"演员的行为不为社会所接受。","D":"剧院上座率正在上升。"},"analysis":{"type":"the RSC deserves no subsidy because 问的是原文给出的具体原因,典型的因果细节题。","parse":"According to the townsfolk, the RSC deserves no subsidy because____ 主干 \"the RSC deserves no subsidy\",According to ... 是状语点明立场,because 后接选项构成原因状语从句,结构平直、无陷阱。","locateEn":"Anyway, the townsfolk can't understand why the Royal Shakespeare Company needs a subsidy. (The theatre has broken attendance records for three years in a row. Last year its 1,431 seats were 94 per cent occupied all year long and this year they'll do better.)","locateZh":"总之,镇民们不理解皇家莎士比亚剧团为何还需要补贴。(剧院连续三年打破上座率纪录;去年 1,431 个座位全年 94% 都有人坐,今年还会更好。)","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"\"涨价可覆盖支出\"是作者/RSC 一方对成本的分析延伸,且原文 It would be a shame to raise prices too much 明确反对涨价;镇民根本没把\"涨价\"作为不该补贴的理由提出。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"通篇没有任何句子说 RSC 财务管理出了问题;镇民只在数票房、不在评管理。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 They frankly dislike the RSC's actors 谈的是镇民讨厌演员的外表与吵闹,不是镇民拿来反对补贴的理由;Q29 问的是补贴话题,不是审美话题。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"镇民给出的\"不需补贴\"的具体证据正是上座率不断走高,与 the theatre attendance is on the rise 完全等价,锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"The theatre has broken attendance records for three years in a row. Last year its 1,431 seats were 94 per cent occupied all year long and this year they'll do better.","opt":"the theatre attendance is on the rise"}]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"From the text we can conclude that the author____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is supportive of both sides."},{"key":"B","text":"favors the townsfolk's view."},{"key":"C","text":"takes a detached attitude."},{"key":"D","text":"is sympathetic to the RSC."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"从文中我们可以得出作者____","choicesZh":{"A":"支持双方。","B":"赞同镇民的观点。","C":"采取超然的态度。","D":"同情RSC。"},"analysis":{"type":"the author____ 后跟的四个选项 is supportive of both sides、favors the townsfolk's view、takes a detached attitude、is sympathetic to the RSC 全是态度极性词,直接定性为态度题。","parse":"From the text we can conclude that the author____ 是 \"From + 状语,we can conclude that + 宾语从句\" 结构,选项做宾语从句的谓语部分,结构清晰。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"作者全文反讽镇民、揭穿其哭穷、不认其抵制补贴的理由,不存在 supportive of both sides 那种均匀支持的笔触。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"作者反讽镇民、揭穿其哭穷、不认其反对补贴的理由,与 favors the townsfolk's view 正好相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"detached attitude 意味中立超然不带感情,但作者用 Nevertheless 的反讽、of course 的语气词、most attractive 的褒义都带有明显情感倾向,谈不上中立。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"三处证据极性一致——反讽镇民 + 为 RSC 解释 + 褒奖 RSC 戏迷——主线只指向一个结论:作者同情 RSC,锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"Nevertheless every hotel in town seems to be adding a new wing or cocktail lounge","opt":"is sympathetic to the RSC"},{"orig":"The reason, of course, is that costs have rocketed and ticket prices have stayed low.","opt":"is sympathetic to the RSC"},{"orig":"the young people who are Stratford's most attractive clientele","opt":"is sympathetic to the RSC"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"When prehistoric man arrived in new parts of the world, something strange happened to the large animals: they suddenly became extinct. Smaller species survived. The large, slow-growing animals were easy game, and were quickly hunted to extinction. Now something similar could be happening in the oceans."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"That the seas are being overfished has been known for years. What researchers such as Ransom Myers and Boris Worm have shown is just how fast things are changing. They have looked at half a century of data from fisheries around the world. Their methods do not attempt to estimate the actual biomass (the amount of living biological matter) of fish species in particular parts of the ocean, but rather changes in that biomass over time. According to their latest paper published in Nature, the biomass of large predators (animals that kill and eat other animals) in a new fishery is reduced on average by 80% within 15 years of the start of exploitation. In some long-fished areas, it has halved again since then."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Dr. Worm acknowledges that these figures are conservative. One reason for this is that fishing technology has improved. Today's vessels can find their prey using satellites and sonar, which were not available 50 years ago. That means a higher proportion of what is in the sea is being caught, so the real difference between present and past is likely to be worse than the one recorded by changes in catch sizes. In the early days, too, longlines would have been more saturated with fish. Some individuals would therefore not have been caught, since no baited hooks would have been available to trap them, leading to an underestimate of fish stocks in the past. Furthermore, in the early days of longline fishing, a lot of fish were lost to sharks after they had been hooked. That is no longer a problem, because there are fewer sharks around now."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"Dr. Myers and Dr. Worm argue that their work gives a correct baseline, which future management efforts must take into account. They believe the data support an idea current among marine biologists, that of the \"shifting baseline\". The notion is that people have failed to detect the massive changes which have happened in the ocean because they have been looking back only a relatively short time into the past. That matters because theory suggests that the maximum sustainable yield that can be cropped from a fishery comes when the biomass of a target species is about 50% of its original levels. Most fisheries are well below that, which is a bad way to do business."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The extinction of large prehistoric animals is noted to suggest that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"large animals were vulnerable to the changing environment."},{"key":"B","text":"small species survived as large animals disappeared."},{"key":"C","text":"large sea animals may face the same threat today."},{"key":"D","text":"slow-growing fish outlive fast-growing ones."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"提到大型史前动物的灭绝是为了表明____","choicesZh":{"A":"大型动物容易受到环境变化的影响。","B":"小型物种在大型动物消失时存活了下来。","C":"大型海洋动物如今可能面临同样的威胁。","D":"生长缓慢的鱼类比生长快速的鱼类寿命更长。"},"analysis":{"type":"The extinction of large prehistoric animals is noted to suggest that 直接给出\"提到 X 是为了说明什么\"的固定问法，正是例证目的题的典型问法。","parse":"The extinction of large prehistoric animals is noted to suggest that 主干是 The extinction is noted to suggest that…，is noted to suggest 是\"被提及以暗示\"的被动结构，that 引出宾语从句作为答案空位；句中无陷阱，只需读懂\"提到史前大动物灭绝这件事，是为了暗示____\"。","locateEn":"Now something similar could be happening in the oceans.","locateZh":"如今，类似的事情可能正发生在海洋里。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"large animals were vulnerable to the changing environment 说大型动物因环境变化而脆弱，但原文给出的原因是 The large, slow-growing animals were easy game, and were quickly hunted to extinction.，是\"被人类捕猎\"而非\"环境变化\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"small species survived as large animals disappeared 复述了 Smaller species survived.，原文确实有，但本题问的是\"提到史前大动物灭绝是为了说明什么\"，不是\"史前发生了什么\"——细节正确却非题干所要。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求答案落在\"今天的海洋大型生物 + 同样威胁 + 可能性\"，C 项三要素齐备，是定位句的同义改写。","pairs":[{"orig":"Now something similar could be happening in the oceans.","opt":"large sea animals may face the same threat today"},{"orig":"in the oceans","opt":"large sea animals"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"slow-growing fish outlive fast-growing ones 说慢生的鱼活得更久，但原文 The large, slow-growing animals were easy game, and were quickly hunted to extinction. 恰恰是\"大型慢生的动物最先被猎杀灭绝\"，方向反了。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"We can infer from Dr. Myers and Dr. Worm's paper that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the stock of large predators in some old fisheries has reduced by 90%."},{"key":"B","text":"there are only half as many fisheries as there were 15 years ago."},{"key":"C","text":"the catch sizes in new fisheries are only 20% of the original amount."},{"key":"D","text":"the number of large predators dropped faster in new fisheries than in the old."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从Myers博士和Worm博士的论文中我们可以推断出____","choicesZh":{"A":"一些老渔场中大型捕食性鱼类的数量已经减少了90%。","B":"现在的渔场数量只有15年前的一半。","C":"新渔场的捕捞量仅为原来的20%。","D":"大型捕食性鱼类的数量在新渔场比在老渔场下降得更快。"},"analysis":{"type":"We can infer from Dr. Myers and Dr. Worm's paper that 明确要求从论文内容推断，属典型推断题。","parse":"We can infer from Dr. Myers and Dr. Worm's paper that 主干是 We can infer that…，from 短语限定信息来源是这篇 paper；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"According to their latest paper published in Nature, the biomass of large predators (animals that kill and eat other animals) in a new fishery is reduced on average by 80% within 15 years of the start of exploitation. In some long-fished areas, it has halved again since then.","locateZh":"根据他们最新发表在《自然》杂志上的论文，新渔场中大型捕食者的生物量在开发开始后的 15 年内平均下降 80%。在某些长期捕捞的水域，自那以后又再减半。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"唯一在\"老渔场\"前提下给出合成结果 90% 的选项，与预判完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"reduced on average by 80% within 15 years of the start of exploitation","opt":"the stock of large predators in some old fisheries has reduced by 90%"},{"orig":"In some long-fished areas","opt":"in some old fisheries"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"there are only half as many fisheries as there were 15 years ago 说渔场数量减半，但原文 it has halved again since then. 中 it 指代 the biomass of large predators（生物量），不是渔场数量。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the catch sizes in new fisheries are only 20% of the original amount 说渔获量只剩原来的 20%，但原文说的是 the biomass of large predators … is reduced on average by 80%——是\"大型捕食者生物量\"减 80%，不是\"渔获量\"。Dr. Worm 在第 3 段更明确指出 real difference between present and past is likely to be worse than the one recorded by changes in catch sizes，明确把 biomass 与 catch sizes 区分开。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the number of large predators dropped faster in new fisheries than in the old 拿新老渔场的下降\"速度\"作比较，但原文只给\"新渔场 15 年降 80%\"与\"老渔场后续再减半\"两个事实，并未比较二者下降速率。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"By saying \"these figures are conservative\" (Line 1, Paragraph 3), Dr. Worm means that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fishing technology has improved rapidly."},{"key":"B","text":"the catch-sizes are actually smaller than recorded."},{"key":"C","text":"the marine biomass has suffered a greater loss."},{"key":"D","text":"the data collected so far are out of date."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"Worm博士说\"这些数字是保守的\"(第3段第1行)意思是____","choicesZh":{"A":"捕鱼技术进步迅速。","B":"捕捞量实际上比记录的要小。","C":"海洋生物量遭受了更大的损失。","D":"迄今收集的数据已经过时。"},"analysis":{"type":"By saying \"these figures are conservative\" (Line 1, Paragraph 3), Dr. Worm means that 是典型的\"作者说 X 意思是\"问法，属词义句意题。","parse":"By saying \"these figures are conservative\" (Line 1, Paragraph 3), Dr. Worm means that 主干是 Dr. Worm means that…，by saying 是方式状语；括号内 (Line 1, Paragraph 3) 是定位线索，不是句子成分；结构无陷阱。","locateEn":"Dr. Worm acknowledges that these figures are conservative. One reason for this is that fishing technology has improved. … That means a higher proportion of what is in the sea is being caught, so the real difference between present and past is likely to be worse than the one recorded by changes in catch sizes.","locateZh":"Worm 博士承认这些数字是保守估计。原因之一是捕鱼技术已经进步……这意味着海里有更高比例的鱼正被捕走，因此当下与过去的真实差距，很可能比渔获量变化所记录的差距还要严重。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"fishing technology has improved rapidly 复述了 fishing technology has improved.，但这只是 Worm 给出的\"为何数字偏低估\"的原因之一，不是 conservative 这个词本身要表达的意思。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the catch-sizes are actually smaller than recorded 说\"渔获量比记录的要小\"，但原文说\"真实损失比记录的渔获量变化反映的更严重\"——是\"生物量损失\"被低估，不是\"渔获量\"本身被低估；catch sizes 在原文里恰恰是用来\"做记录\"的工具，不是被低估的对象。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"唯一指向\"真实损失比记录的更大\"的选项，正是 conservative 一词在本段的工作义。","pairs":[{"orig":"the real difference between present and past is likely to be worse than the one recorded by changes in catch sizes","opt":"the marine biomass has suffered a greater loss"},{"orig":"these figures are conservative","opt":"the marine biomass has suffered a greater loss"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the data collected so far are out of date 说数据\"过时\"，但原文从未提及数据时效性，只说数据偏低估——\"低估\"与\"过时\"是两回事。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"Dr. Myers and other researchers hold that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"people should look for a baseline that can work for a longer time."},{"key":"B","text":"fisheries should keep their yields below 50% of the biomass."},{"key":"C","text":"the ocean biomass should be restored to its original level."},{"key":"D","text":"people should adjust the fishing baseline to the changing situation."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Myers博士和其他研究人员认为____","choicesZh":{"A":"人们应该寻找一个可以长期有效的基准线。","B":"渔场应该将捕获量保持在生物量的50%以下。","C":"海洋生物量应该恢复到其原来的水平。","D":"人们应该根据变化的情况调整捕鱼基准线。"},"analysis":{"type":"Dr. Myers and other researchers hold that 问\"他们主张什么\"，答案就写在原文相应观点句里，属立场归属型细节题。","parse":"Dr. Myers and other researchers hold that 主干是 Dr. Myers and other researchers hold that…，hold that 引出宾语从句，宾语就是答案空位；句式平实，无陷阱。","locateEn":"They believe the data support an idea current among marine biologists, that of the \"shifting baseline\". The notion is that people have failed to detect the massive changes which have happened in the ocean because they have been looking back only a relatively short time into the past.","locateZh":"他们认为这些数据支持海洋生物学界当前流行的\"基线漂移\"观点。其要旨是：人们之所以未能察觉海洋中已经发生的巨大变化，是因为他们回望的时间太短。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"people should look for a baseline that can work for a longer time 说要找\"能用更长时间的基线\"，但原文主张的不是\"基线要长寿\"，而是\"基线参考的回望时段要拉长 / 要随变化漂移\"；longer time 偷换了 shifting 的方向。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"fisheries should keep their yields below 50% of the biomass 说\"渔获量应低于生物量的 50%\"，但原文 the maximum sustainable yield … comes when the biomass of a target species is about 50% of its original levels 说的是\"当目标物种生物量为原始水平的 50% 时，可持续捕捞量最大\"——50% 指生物量与原始量之比，不是渔获与生物量之比，且原文是\"维持在 50% 左右\"，不是\"低于 50%\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the ocean biomass should be restored to its original level 说应把海洋生物量恢复到原始水平，但原文只说\"生物量维持在原始量的约 50% 时可持续捕捞量最大\"，从未主张\"恢复到 100%\"；这是把数据观察直接拔高到管理目标。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"唯一抓住\"基线随情况而调整\"语义的选项，与定位句的核心主张一一对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"the \"shifting baseline\"","opt":"people should adjust the fishing baseline to the changing situation"},{"orig":"people have failed to detect the massive changes which have happened in the ocean because they have been looking back only a relatively short time into the past","opt":"adjust the fishing baseline to the changing situation"}]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"The author seems to be mainly concerned with most fisheries'____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"management efficiency."},{"key":"B","text":"biomass level."},{"key":"C","text":"catch-size limits."},{"key":"D","text":"technological application."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"作者似乎主要关注大多数渔场的____","choicesZh":{"A":"管理效率。","B":"生物量水平。","C":"捕捞量限制。","D":"技术应用。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author seems to be mainly concerned with most fisheries' 用 mainly concerned with 直接问作者主要关注什么，是典型主旨题问法。","parse":"The author seems to be mainly concerned with most fisheries' 主干是 The author seems to be concerned with…，mainly 是程度修饰，most fisheries' 后省略了名词中心（即答案选项填入的那个名词），全句相当于\"作者似乎主要关心的是大多数渔场的____\"；属于第一步说明里提到的\"题干是待补全的不完整陈述句，选项是延续\"的形态。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"management efficiency 说\"管理效率\"，但全文核心是数据所揭示的\"生物量大幅下降被低估\"，future management efforts must take into account 只是顺带提到管理应以此为参照，不是作者主要关切。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"唯一既覆盖第 2、3、4 段中心术语 biomass、又对得上末段态度焦点的选项，是主线的一词归结。","pairs":[{"orig":"Most fisheries are well below that, which is a bad way to do business.","opt":"biomass level"},{"orig":"the biomass of large predators (animals that kill and eat other animals) in a new fishery is reduced on average by 80% within 15 years of the start of exploitation","opt":"biomass level"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"catch-size limits 说\"渔获量限额\"，但原文里 catch sizes 出现是用来说明\"靠渔获量记录会低估损失\"，并不讨论该不该设上限；这是把术语挪用为不存在的话题。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"technological application 说\"技术应用\"，但 fishing technology has improved 只是 Worm 解释\"为什么数字偏低估\"的三条原因之一，是支线证据，不是作者主要关切。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Many things make people think artists are weird. But the weirdest may be this: artists' only job is to explore emotions, and yet they choose to focus on the ones that feel bad."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"This wasn't always so. The earliest forms of art, like painting and music, are those best suited for expressing joy. But somewhere from the 19th century onward, more artists began seeing happiness as meaningless, phony or, worst of all, boring, as we went from Wordsworth's daffodils to Baudelaire's flowers of evil."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"You could argue that art became more skeptical of happiness because modern times have seen so much misery. But it's not as if earlier times didn't know perpetual war, disaster and the massacre of innocents. The reason, in fact, may be just the opposite: there is too much damn happiness in the world today."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"After all, what is the one modern form of expression almost completely dedicated to depicting happiness? Advertising. The rise of anti-happy art almost exactly tracks the emergence of mass media, and with it, a commercial culture in which happiness is not just an ideal but an ideology."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"People in earlier eras were surrounded by reminders of misery. They worked until exhausted, lived with few protections and died young. In the West, before mass communication and literacy, the most powerful mass medium was the church, which reminded worshippers that their souls were in danger and that they would someday be meat for worms. Given all this, they did not exactly need their art to be a bummer too."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"Today the messages the average Westerner is surrounded with are not religious but commercial, and forever happy. Fast-food eaters, news anchors, text messengers, all smiling, smiling, smiling. Our magazines feature beaming celebrities and happy families in perfect homes. And since these messages have an agenda – to lure us to open our wallets – they make the very idea of happiness seem unreliable. \"Celebrate!\" commanded the ads for the arthritis drug Celebrex, before we found out it could increase the risk of heart attacks."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"But what we forget – what our economy depends on us forgetting – is that happiness is more than pleasure without pain. The things that bring the greatest joy carry the greatest potential for loss and disappointment. Today, surrounded by promises of easy happiness, we need art to tell us, as religion once did, Memento mori: remember that you will die, that everything ends, and that happiness comes not in denying this but in living with it. It's a message even more bitter than a clove cigarette, yet, somehow, a breath of fresh air."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"By citing the examples of poets Wordsworth and Baudelaire, the author intends to show that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"poetry is not as expressive of joy as painting or music."},{"key":"B","text":"art grows out of both positive and negative feelings."},{"key":"C","text":"poets today are less skeptical of happiness."},{"key":"D","text":"artists have changed their focus of interest."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"通过引用诗人Wordsworth和Baudelaire的例子,作者意图表明____","choicesZh":{"A":"诗歌在表达快乐方面不如绘画或音乐。","B":"艺术源于积极和消极两种情感。","C":"当今诗人对幸福的怀疑态度有所减少。","D":"艺术家已经改变了他们的兴趣焦点。"},"analysis":{"type":"By citing the examples of poets Wordsworth and Baudelaire, the author intends to show that 明示作者举例的用意，正是例证目的题的标准句式。","parse":"句子主干是 the author intends to show that，前面 By citing the examples of poets Wordsworth and Baudelaire 是 by 引导的方式状语，that 后接选项作宾语从句。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱，只要看清主干在问\"作者想说明什么\"即可。","locateEn":"But somewhere from the 19th century onward, more artists began seeing happiness as meaningless, phony or, worst of all, boring, as we went from Wordsworth's daffodils to Baudelaire's flowers of evil.","locateZh":"但从十九世纪某个时点起，越来越多的艺术家开始把幸福看作无意义、虚假，乃至最糟的——无聊；我们由此从华兹华斯的水仙走到了波德莱尔的恶之花。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"poetry is not as expressive of joy as painting or music 把诗与画/乐做\"抒发喜悦能力\"的横向比较，原文从未出现，属凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"art grows out of both positive and negative feelings 强调\"正负情感都生发艺术\"，但原文 more artists began seeing happiness as meaningless 描述的是单向转变，并不主张二者并存。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文是 more artists began seeing happiness as meaningless, phony … boring——更怀疑幸福，而 poets today are less skeptical of happiness 说\"今天更不怀疑\"，正好与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"关注焦点变了\"与 artists have changed their focus of interest 高度吻合，故锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"more artists began seeing happiness as meaningless, phony or, worst of all, boring","opt":"artists have changed their focus of interest"},{"orig":"we went from Wordsworth's daffodils to Baudelaire's flowers of evil","opt":"changed their focus of interest"}]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"The word \"bummer\" (Line 5, Paragraph 5) most probably means something____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"religious."},{"key":"B","text":"unpleasant."},{"key":"C","text":"entertaining."},{"key":"D","text":"commercial."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"单词\"bummer\"(第5段第5行)最可能指某种____的事物","choicesZh":{"A":"宗教性的。","B":"令人不快的。","C":"娱乐性的。","D":"商业性的。"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"bummer\" (Line 5, Paragraph 5) most probably means something 含 means，标准词义题问法。","parse":"题干主干 The word \"bummer\" … most probably means something____，括号内 (Line 5, Paragraph 5) 是定位辅助；选项填在 something 后做后置定语。结构无陷阱。","locateEn":"Given all this, they did not exactly need their art to be a bummer too.","locateZh":"鉴于这一切，他们也并不真需要自己的艺术再来当一个 bummer（扫兴的东西）。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"religious 取自上文 the church, which reminded worshippers that their souls were in danger 的话题词，但 bummer 是\"不需要让艺术也来当\"的对象，与\"宗教性\"在词义上不等值。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"令人不快\"与 unpleasant 在极性（负）与词性（形容词描述状态）上完全一致，锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"they did not exactly need their art to be a bummer too","opt":"unpleasant"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"entertaining 是正面词\"令人愉快的\"，而上下文 Given all this, they did not exactly need their art to be a bummer too 中 too 把 bummer 拉到负面序列，极性正好相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"commercial 的语境在第 6 段 Today the messages the average Westerner is surrounded with are not religious but commercial，与第 5 段 bummer 所在的苦难语境不在同一区段，且极性是中性—正面，不匹配。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"In the author's opinion, advertising____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"emerges in the wake of the anti-happy art."},{"key":"B","text":"is a cause of disappointment for the general public."},{"key":"C","text":"replaces the church as a major source of information."},{"key":"D","text":"creates an illusion of happiness rather than happiness itself."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在作者看来,广告____","choicesZh":{"A":"在反幸福艺术之后出现。","B":"是公众失望的一个原因。","C":"取代教会成为主要的信息来源。","D":"创造了幸福的幻觉而非幸福本身。"},"analysis":{"type":"In the author's opinion, advertising____ 问的是作者对一个具体对象（广告）的看法，无 infer/imply，属于直接读出观点的细节题。","parse":"主干 advertising____，In the author's opinion 为插入状语限定视角；选项作谓语补全句子。结构无陷阱，但要记住答案必须是作者立场，不是广告业的自我宣传。","locateEn":"The rise of anti-happy art almost exactly tracks the emergence of mass media, and with it, a commercial culture in which happiness is not just an ideal but an ideology.","locateZh":"反幸福艺术的兴起几乎正好与大众媒体的出现同步，随之而来的是一种商业文化——在其中，幸福不只是一种理想，更是一种意识形态。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"emerges in the wake of the anti-happy art 说广告\"在反幸福艺术之后兴起\"，但原文 The rise of anti-happy art almost exactly tracks the emergence of mass media 是反幸福艺术追随大众媒体（广告）兴起，方向正好相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"is a cause of disappointment for the general public 把广告说成\"令大众失望的根源\"，但原文 they make the very idea of happiness seem unreliable 说的是它让\"幸福这个概念\"显得不可信，并未论及大众的失望情绪。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"replaces the church as a major source of information 主张广告取代教会成为主要信息源；原文 Today the messages the average Westerner is surrounded with are not religious but commercial 只是说\"如今信息从宗教变成商业\"，未明确广告取代了教会作为\"information source\"的地位，过度引申。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"广告卖的是幸福假象\"与 creates an illusion of happiness rather than happiness itself 完全吻合，锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"happiness is not just an ideal but an ideology","opt":"creates an illusion of happiness rather than happiness itself"},{"orig":"they make the very idea of happiness seem unreliable","opt":"an illusion of happiness"}]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"We can learn from the last paragraph that the author believes____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"happiness more often than not ends in sadness."},{"key":"B","text":"the anti-happy art is distasteful but refreshing."},{"key":"C","text":"misery should be enjoyed rather than denied."},{"key":"D","text":"the anti-happy art flourishes when economy booms."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"我们可以从最后一段得知作者认为____","choicesZh":{"A":"幸福往往以悲伤告终。","B":"反幸福艺术令人不快但却令人耳目一新。","C":"痛苦应该被享受而非被否认。","D":"反幸福艺术在经济繁荣时兴盛。"},"analysis":{"type":"We can learn from the last paragraph that the author believes____ 虽含 learn from，但定位段已固定，问的是段内作者明示的看法，按细节题做最稳。","parse":"主干 the author believes____，We can learn from the last paragraph that 是引导宾语从句的框架。结构无陷阱。","locateEn":"It's a message even more bitter than a clove cigarette, yet, somehow, a breath of fresh air.","locateZh":"这是一条比丁香烟还要苦的讯息，然而，不知怎的，又像一口新鲜空气。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"happiness more often than not ends in sadness 说\"幸福十有八九以悲伤收场\"，是绝对化判断；原文 The things that bring the greatest joy carry the greatest potential for loss and disappointment 只说\"带有最大的失落\"潜在性\"\"，并未断言概率上必然如此。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"虽苦但提神\"与 the anti-happy art is distasteful but refreshing 在两面并存的结构与对应词上完全吻合，锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"even more bitter than a clove cigarette","opt":"distasteful"},{"orig":"a breath of fresh air","opt":"refreshing"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"misery should be enjoyed rather than denied 说苦难应被\"享受\"而非\"否认\"，但原文 happiness comes not in denying this but in living with it 主张\"与之共存\"——live with it 不是 enjoy it，更不是叫人去享受痛苦。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the anti-happy art flourishes when economy booms 主张\"经济繁荣时反幸福艺术兴盛\"，本段乃至全文都未谈经济景气周期与艺术繁荣的关联，纯属凭空捏造。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"Which of the following is true of the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Religion once functioned as a reminder of misery."},{"key":"B","text":"Art provides a balance between expectation and reality."},{"key":"C","text":"People feel disappointed at the realities of modern society."},{"key":"D","text":"Mass media are inclined to cover disasters and deaths."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"以下哪一项关于本文的表述是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"宗教曾起到提醒痛苦的作用。","B":"艺术在期望与现实之间提供平衡。","C":"人们对现代社会的现实感到失望。","D":"大众媒体倾向于报道灾难和死亡。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of the text? 要求选项与原文事实一致，是典型的判断符合题（细节题的一种）。","parse":"题干一句话疑问句，主干 Which of the following is true of the text?，无从句、无否定，结构平铺直叙。","locateEn":"In the West, before mass communication and literacy, the most powerful mass medium was the church, which reminded worshippers that their souls were in danger and that they would someday be meat for worms.","locateZh":"在西方，大众传播与识字普及之前，最强大的大众媒介是教会——它提醒信众，他们的灵魂处于危险之中，他们将来终有一日会成为蛆虫的食物。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"宗教曾作为苦难提醒\"与 Religion once functioned as a reminder of misery 三处等值（remind→reminder、church→religion、before…→once），锁定 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"the church, which reminded worshippers that their souls were in danger and that they would someday be meat for worms","opt":"Religion once functioned as a reminder of misery"},{"orig":"the most powerful mass medium was the church","opt":"Religion"},{"orig":"before mass communication and literacy","opt":"once"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Art provides a balance between expectation and reality 说艺术\"在期望与现实间提供平衡\"，但原文 happiness comes not in denying this but in living with it 谈的是\"与死亡/无常共存\"，并未谈\"期望—现实\"的对立平衡，凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"People feel disappointed at the realities of modern society 说\"人们对现代社会的现实感到失望\"，但原文 they make the very idea of happiness seem unreliable 只说幸福概念变得可疑，并未给出大众普遍\"失望\"的情绪判断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Mass media are inclined to cover disasters and deaths 说大众媒介\"倾向报道灾难与死亡\"，但原文 Today the messages the average Westerner is surrounded with are not religious but commercial, and forever happy 明确说今日大众媒介\"forever happy\"，方向正相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"matching","title":"Section II Part B 选句填空","directions":"Directions: In the following article, some sentences have been removed. For Questions 41-45, choose the most suitable one from the list A-G to fit into each of numbered gaps. There are two extra choices, which you do not need to use. Mark your answers on ANSWER SHEET 1. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"On the north bank of the Ohio river sits Evansville, Ind., home of David Williams, 52, and of a riverboat casino (a place where gambling games are played). During several years of gambling in that casino, Williams, a state auditor earning $35,000 a year, lost approximately $175,000. He had never gambled before the casino sent him a coupon for $20 worth of gambling."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"He visited the casino, lost the $20 and left. On his second visit he lost $800. The casino issued to him, as a good customer, a \"Fun Card,\" which when used in the casino earns points for meals and drinks, and enables the casino to track the user's gambling activities. For Williams, those activities became what he calls \"electronic heroin.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"{{41}} In 1997 he lost $21,000 to one slot machine in two days. In March 1997 he lost $72,186. He sometimes played two slot machines at a time, all night, until the boat docked at 5 a.m., then went back aboard when the casino opened at 9 a.m. Now he is suing the casino, charging that it should have refused his patronage because it knew he was addicted. It did know he had a problem."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"In March 1998, a friend of Williams's got him involuntarily confined to a treatment center for addictions, and wrote to inform the casino of Williams's gambling problem. The casino included a photo of Williams among those of banned gamblers, and wrote to him a \"cease admissions\" letter. Noting the \"medical/psychological\" nature of problem gambling behavior, the letter said that before being readmitted to the casino he would have to present medical/psychological information demonstrating that patronizing the casino would pose no threat to his safety or well-being."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"{{42}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"The Wall Street Journal reports that the casino has 24 signs warning: \"Enjoy the fun…and always bet with your head, not over it.\" Every entrance ticket lists a toll-free number for counseling from the Indiana Department of Mental Health. Nevertheless, Williams's suit charges that the casino, knowing he was \"helplessly addicted to gambling,\" intentionally worked to \"lure\" him to \"engage in conduct against his will.\" Well."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"","text":"{{43}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-8","label":"","text":"The fourth edition of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders says \"pathological gambling\" involves persistent, recurring and uncontrollable pursuit less of money than of the thrill of taking risks in quest of a windfall."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-9","label":"","text":"{{44}} Pushed by science, or what claims to be science, society is reclassifying what once were considered character flaws or moral failings as personality disorders akin to physical disabilities."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-10","label":"","text":"{{45}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-11","label":"","text":"Forty-four states have lotteries, 29 have casinos, and most of these states are to varying degrees dependent on – you might say addicted to – revenues from wagering. And since the first Internet gambling site was created in 1995, competition for gamblers' dollars has become intense. The Oct. 28 issue of Newsweek reported that 2 million gamblers patronize 1,800 virtual casinos every week. With $3.5 billion being lost on Internet wagers this year, gambling has passed pornography as the Web's most profitable business."}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected."},{"key":"B","text":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?"},{"key":"C","text":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit."},{"key":"D","text":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government."},{"key":"E","text":"David Williams's suit should trouble this gambling nation. But don't bet on it."},{"key":"F","text":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will."},{"key":"G","text":"The anonymous, lonely, undistracted nature of online gambling is especially conducive to compulsive behavior. But even if the government knew how to move against Internet gambling, what would be its grounds for doing so?"}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected."},{"key":"B","text":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?"},{"key":"C","text":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit."},{"key":"D","text":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government."},{"key":"E","text":"David Williams's suit should trouble this gambling nation. But don't bet on it."},{"key":"F","text":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will."},{"key":"G","text":"The anonymous, lonely, undistracted nature of online gambling is especially conducive to compulsive behavior. But even if the government knew how to move against Internet gambling, what would be its grounds for doing so?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"段首","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit. 当他输掉5000美元时,他对自己说如果能回本就收手。一天晚上他赢了5500美元,但他没有收手。\n承接\"上瘾\"、引出越输越大的金额时间线 空 41 在第 3 段段首，紧挨着的下文是 In 1997 he lost $21,000 to one slot machine in two days. In March 1997 he lost $72,186.——下文是一串越来越大的输钱金额与具体时间。上一段末已把他的赌博称作 electronic heroin。因此这个段首空要补一句承上启下的话：承\"他已陷入电子海洛因般的上瘾\"，启下文\"输得越来越多\"的金额叙事，自身也应是 Williams 沉沦过程里时间更早、数额更小的一环。\n数字 $5,000/$5,500 正好排在 $21,000 之前，he 承接主人公 By the time he had lost $5,000 的数额小于下文 he lost $21,000，正好处于递增金额链的更前端，时序上对得上；主语 he 承接 Williams 无需新先行词；but he did not quit 表明他停不下来，恰好引出后文越输越多，承上启下双向缝合。","options":{},"choiceEn":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit.","clues":["词汇复现 金额数字链：下文 $21,000、$72,186 下文 In 1997 he lost $21,000、In March 1997 he lost $72,186 是一串递增的输钱数字。这条线索要求正确句也带金额数字，且数额应明显小于 $21,000，从而排在这条递增链的更前端。","代词指代 全程 he 指 Williams，无需新先行词 本段下文 he lost $21,000 一路用 he 承接前文主人公 Williams。这条线索要求正确句的主语也是承接性的 he，叙述的仍是 Williams 本人，而非另起人物或宏观议论。"]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected."},{"key":"B","text":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?"},{"key":"C","text":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit."},{"key":"D","text":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government."},{"key":"E","text":"David Williams's suit should trouble this gambling nation. But don't bet on it."},{"key":"F","text":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will."},{"key":"G","text":"The anonymous, lonely, undistracted nature of online gambling is especially conducive to compulsive behavior. But even if the government knew how to move against Internet gambling, what would be its grounds for doing so?"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"独占整段","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected. 尽管没有提供此类证据,赌场的营销部门仍继续向他邮寄广告材料。他进入赌场并使用他的Fun Card而未被察觉。\n承接赌场禁令\"需提供医学证据\"，写后续如何收场 空 42 独占第 5 段，前一段(第 4 段)末尾刚说赌场发了禁入信，要求他 present medical/psychological information demonstrating that patronizing the casino would pose no threat；后一段(第 6 段)开头转而说 the casino has 24 signs warning。这个独占整段的空夹在二者之间，应补一句过渡/小结：交代上文那道\"需提交医学证据\"的禁令后来怎样了。\nAlthough + no such evidence 精准回指前段证据要求，且 Fun Card 复现 Although no such evidence was presented 用 such 回指前段要求的 medical/psychological information，让步逻辑直承禁令；the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings 和 he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected 写出\"禁令形同虚设、他照样进场\"，既接上前段、又为后段他能继续赌、进而起诉埋下事实，双向缝合。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected.","clues":["代词指代 前段提出的\"医学证据\"是后文 such evidence 的先行说法 前段 he would have to present medical/psychological information 抛出了\"需提供医学/心理证据\"这一要求。这条线索要求正确句能用一个回指词承接\"这种证据\"，即句中应出现指代该证据的说法，紧扣前段的禁令条件。","逻辑连接 禁令\"要求证据\"与实际\"他照样进场\"形成让步反差 前段是赌场摆出严格的禁入条件 before being readmitted to the casino he would have to present medical/psychological information，后段却讲赌场设了警示牌仍被起诉。这条线索要求正确句带让步逻辑：尽管证据没拿出，赌场却仍照旧待他、他也照旧能进。"]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected."},{"key":"B","text":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?"},{"key":"C","text":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit."},{"key":"D","text":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government."},{"key":"E","text":"David Williams's suit should trouble this gambling nation. But don't bet on it."},{"key":"F","text":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will."},{"key":"G","text":"The anonymous, lonely, undistracted nature of online gambling is especially conducive to compulsive behavior. But even if the government knew how to move against Internet gambling, what would be its grounds for doing so?"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"独占整段","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative? 鉴于他的强迫性行为,尚不清楚需要什么样的诱惑。而且他的意志在何种意义上起作用?\n承上文\"引诱、违背意志\"的指控，转入作者质疑 空 43 独占第 7 段，前一段(第 6 段)末尾是 Williams 指控赌场 intentionally worked to \"lure\" him to \"engage in conduct against his will.\"，并以一句意味深长的 Well. 收尾；后一段(第 8 段)转入 pathological gambling 的官方病理定义。这个独占整段的空应补一句作者亲自下场质疑的话：顺着 Well 的语气，反驳\"引诱、违背意志\"之说。\nluring、will 逐词回扣前段指控，反问句承 Well 反驳口吻 It is unclear what luring was required 回扣前段 \"lure\"，in what sense was his will operative? 回扣 against his will；两句反问紧承 Well. 的语气，正是作者反驳\"赌场引诱、违背其意志\"之说。复现词对上、逻辑口吻对上，落点精准。","options":{},"choiceEn":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?","clues":["词汇复现 前段指控用词 lure、will 需被正确句回扣 前段指控里出现了 \"lure\" 和 against his will 两个关键词。这条线索要求正确句直接回扣这两个词(以 luring/will 等形式再现)，从而构成对该指控的针对性回应。","逻辑连接 Well 之后应是作者反驳，正确句须带质疑口吻 前段末 Well. 是作者欲言又止、转入反驳的信号。这条线索要求正确句带怀疑、反问的逻辑：质疑\"既已强迫成瘾，还谈何引诱、谈何意志\"，与作者对原告说法的保留态度一致。"]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected."},{"key":"B","text":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?"},{"key":"C","text":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit."},{"key":"D","text":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government."},{"key":"E","text":"David Williams's suit should trouble this gambling nation. But don't bet on it."},{"key":"F","text":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will."},{"key":"G","text":"The anonymous, lonely, undistracted nature of online gambling is especially conducive to compulsive behavior. But even if the government knew how to move against Internet gambling, what would be its grounds for doing so?"}],"answer":"F","explanation":{"answer":"F","type":"段首","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will. 令人担忧的是,社会正在将越来越多的行为问题医学化,常常将早期更严格的几代人解释为意志薄弱的问题定义为成瘾。\n承上文病理定义，引出对\"医学化\"现象的忧虑 空 44 在第 9 段段首，紧接其后的下文是 Pushed by science, or what claims to be science, society is reclassifying what once were considered character flaws or moral failings as personality disorders——讲社会把昔日的道德缺陷重新归类为人格障碍。上一段(第 8 段)刚给出 pathological gambling 的官方病理定义。这个段首空要补一句总起：承\"赌博被定为病理\"，启下文\"社会正把恶习重新归类为疾病\"，且应亮明作者对此的态度。\nmedicalizing/weakness of will 同义复现下句论断，worrisome 表态 society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems 与下句 society is reclassifying 同义，weakness of will 对应 character flaws or moral failings、addictions 对应 personality disorders，是标准的同义总起；It is worrisome 又亮明作者忧虑的态度，恰好承担议论段段首的总起兼表态功能。","options":{},"choiceEn":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will.","clues":["词汇复现 下句 reclassifying…character flaws…as personality disorders 的同义说法 下文 society is reclassifying what once were considered character flaws or moral failings as personality disorders 是核心论断。这条线索要求正确句以同义方式复现它：把\"昔日视为意志/品行问题的东西，如今定性为病/瘾\"这层意思换一种说法先总起。","结构功能 段首总起 + 表态，需带评价词 9 段是作者亮明立场的议论段，段首 Pushed by science 之前的空承担\"提出本段主张并表态\"的功能。这条线索要求正确句不只是客观陈述，还要带作者的评价(忧虑/质疑)，与全文对\"医学化\"的保留态度一致。"]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Although no such evidence was presented, the casino's marketing department continued to pepper him with mailings. And he entered the casino and used his Fun Card without being detected."},{"key":"B","text":"It is unclear what luring was required, given his compulsive behavior. And in what sense was his will operative?"},{"key":"C","text":"By the time he had lost $5,000 he said to himself that if he could get back to even, he would quit. One night he won $5,500, but he did not quit."},{"key":"D","text":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government."},{"key":"E","text":"David Williams's suit should trouble this gambling nation. But don't bet on it."},{"key":"F","text":"It is worrisome that society is medicalizing more and more behavioral problems, often defining as addictions what earlier, sterner generations explained as weakness of will."},{"key":"G","text":"The anonymous, lonely, undistracted nature of online gambling is especially conducive to compulsive behavior. But even if the government knew how to move against Internet gambling, what would be its grounds for doing so?"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"独占整段","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government. 赌博一直是美国生活的常见特征,但长期以来它被广泛认为是一种罪恶或社会疾病。现在它是一项社会政策:美国最重要且最积极的赌博推动者是政府。\n引出\"赌博成社会政策、政府是推手\"，开启末段政府话题 空 45 独占第 10 段，后一段(第 11 段)开头是 Forty-four states have lotteries, 29 have casinos, and most of these states are to varying degrees dependent on – you might say addicted to – revenues from wagering.——讲各州政府靠博彩收入、乃至\"上瘾\"。前一段(第 9 段)谈的是社会把恶习病理化。这个独占整段的空应补一句过渡兼总起：把话题从\"病理化\"转到\"政府/各州依赖赌博收入\"，并点出政府这一新焦点。\n句末 the government 正引出下段各州数据，过去 vs 如今完成话题切换 Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government. 句末抛出 the government，正好被下段 Forty-four states have lotteries, 29 have casinos 用各州数据接住展开；but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin 到 Now it is a social policy 的古今对比，是宏观主题句的口吻，承上启下成立。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Gambling has been a common feature of American life forever, but for a long time it was broadly considered a sin, or a social disease. Now it is a social policy: the most important and aggressive promoter of gambling in America is the government.","clues":["词汇复现 后段 states…revenues from wagering 指向\"政府\"，正确句须先抛出 后文 most of these states are to varying degrees dependent on – you might say addicted to – revenues from wagering 大谈各州政府依赖博彩收入。这条线索要求正确句先抛出\"政府是赌博推手\"这一说法，为下文 states 的展开提供先行话题。","结构功能 独占整段作过渡兼末段总起 45 空独占一段、且后接全文最后一段的具体数据。这条线索要求正确句承担\"承上(病理化议题)、启下(政府/各州数据)\"的过渡总起功能，宜是宏观对比式的主题句，而非细节句。"]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"Is it true that the American intellectual is rejected and considered of no account in his society? I am going to suggest that it is not true. Father Bruckberger told part of the story when he observed that it is the intellectuals who have rejected America. But they have done more than that. They have grown dissatisfied with the role of the intellectual. It is they, not America, who have become anti-intellectual."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"First, the object of our study pleads for definition. What is an intellectual? (46) I shall define him as an individual who has elected as his primary duty and pleasure in life the activity of thinking in a Socratic(苏格拉底) way about moral problems. He explores such problems consciously, articulately, and frankly, first by asking factual questions, then by asking moral questions, finally by suggesting action which seems appropriate in the light of the factual and moral information which he has obtained. (47) His function is analogous to that of a judge, who must accept the obligation of revealing in as obvious a manner as possible the course of reasoning which led him to his decision."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"This definition excludes many individuals usually referred to as intellectuals – the average scientist, for one. (48) I have excluded him because, while his accomplishments may contribute to the solution of moral problems, he has not been charged with the task of approaching any but the factual aspects of those problems. Like other human beings, he encounters moral issues even in the everyday performance of his routine duties – he is not supposed to cook his experiments, manufacture evidence, or doctor his reports. (49) But his primary task is not to think about the moral code which governs his activity, any more than a businessman is expected to dedicate his energies to an exploration of rules of conduct in business. During most of his waking life he will take his code for granted, as the businessman takes his ethics."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-4","text":"The definition also excludes the majority of teachers, despite the fact that teaching has traditionally been the method whereby many intellectuals earn their living. (50) They may teach very well, and more than earn their salaries, but most of them make little or no independent reflections on human problems which involve moral judgment. This description even fits the majority of eminent scholars. Being learned in some branch of human knowledge is one thing: living in \"public and illustrious thoughts,\" as Emerson would say, is something else."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"I shall define him as an individual who has elected as his primary duty and pleasure in life the activity of thinking in a Socratic(苏格拉底) way about moral problems.","refZh":"我将把这样的人定义为知识分子：他把以苏格拉底的方式思考道德问题这一活动，选作自己人生中首要的责任与乐趣。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"I shall define him as an individual","lit":"我将把他定义为这样一个人","role":"（主干：主谓宾 + as 宾补）","note":"难点： him 回指「知识分子」 him 不是泛指的「他」，而是承接上一句 What is an intellectual? 的话题。译文里第一次出现就应显化为「知识分子」，或译成「我将给知识分子下这样一个定义」，避免读者不知道在定义谁。"},{"en":"who has elected as his primary duty and pleasure in life","lit":"他把……选作自己人生中首要的责任与乐趣","role":"（who 引导的定语从句（主干部分）+ as 短语作宾补前置）","note":"难点： elect A as B 的语序倒装 正常语序是 elect [the activity of thinking…] as [his primary duty and pleasure in life]，因为真正的宾语（the activity…）太长，被挪到了句末，as 短语先出现。翻译时必须把后面的 the activity… 调回来当 elect 的宾语，否则会译成不知所云的「他选了作为他的首要责任与乐趣」。elect 此处取「选定、选作」，不是「选举」。"},{"en":"the activity of thinking in a Socratic(苏格拉底) way about moral problems.","lit":"以苏格拉底的方式思考道德问题这一活动","role":"（elect 的真正宾语（被后置））","note":"难点： of + 动名词短语作同位语 / 抽象名词具体化 the activity of thinking… 直译「思考……这一活动」读起来很翻译腔，可具体化为「以苏格拉底的方式思考道德问题」这一动作本身。Socratic 已给出「苏格拉底（式）」的提示，统一译为「以苏格拉底的方式」或「以苏格拉底式的方式」。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"His function is analogous to that of a judge, who must accept the obligation of revealing in as obvious a manner as possible the course of reasoning which led him to his decision.","refZh":"知识分子的作用类似于法官的作用：法官必须承担这样一项义务——以尽可能明白的方式，把自己做出判决所依据的推理过程揭示出来。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"His function is analogous to that of a judge,","lit":"他的作用类似于法官的作用","role":"（主干：主系表 + 比较）","note":"难点： that 代替 function 避免重复 that of a judge 中的 that 是替代词，代替前文的 function，避免说 the function of a judge。翻译时直接补出「作用/职责」，译成「类似于法官的作用/职责」。His 仍回指「知识分子」。"},{"en":"who must accept the obligation of revealing","lit":"他必须承担揭示……的义务","role":"（who 引导的非限制性定语从句（说明 judge））","note":"难点： 非限制性定从→另起一句 who 前有逗号，是非限制性定语从句，对 judge 作补充说明。汉语里不要硬译成「必须承担义务的法官」，应另起一句「法官必须承担……的义务」，更符合中文「短句串联」的节奏。"},{"en":"in as obvious a manner as possible","lit":"以尽可能明显的方式","role":"（方式状语（修饰 revealing））","note":"难点： as + adj + a + n + as possible 的同等比较结构 这是「as + 形容词 + a/an + 名词 + as possible」的固定结构，等价于 in a manner as obvious as possible。整体意为「以尽可能 X 的方式」。此处 obvious 译「明白/清楚」比「明显」更贴近「把推理过程让人看得明明白白」的语境。这是该句最容易翻丢的采分点。"},{"en":"the course of reasoning which led him to his decision.","lit":"把他引向他的判决的推理过程","role":"（revealing 的宾语（含 which 定语从句））","note":"难点： course of reasoning 与 led…to…decision 的法律语境 course of reasoning 意为「推理过程 / 推理思路」；judge 语境下 decision 指「判决/裁决」而非泛指「决定」。which led him to his decision 是修饰 reasoning 的定语从句，译为「使他做出判决的」前置即可。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"I have excluded him because, while his accomplishments may contribute to the solution of moral problems, he has not been charged with the task of approaching any but the factual aspects of those problems.","refZh":"我之所以把普通科学家排除在外，是因为：尽管他的研究成果可能有助于解决道德问题，但他并没有被赋予这样的任务——去探究这些问题中除事实层面以外的其他方面。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"I have excluded him","lit":"我把他排除在外","role":"（主干：主谓宾）","note":"难点： him = the average scientist（普通科学家） him 回指上一句 This definition excludes many individuals usually referred to as intellectuals – the average scientist, for one. 中的 the average scientist。翻译时显化为「我之所以把普通科学家（这种人）排除在外」，避免读者读到「我把他排除在外」时一头雾水。"},{"en":"because, while his accomplishments may contribute to the solution of moral problems,","lit":"因为，虽然他的成就可能有助于解决道德问题，","role":"（原因状语从句中嵌套的让步状语从句）","note":"难点： while 此处是「虽然」不是「当……的时候」 while 后接的主句是 he has not been charged…（与之形成对比/转折），所以 while 在这里是让步连词「虽然/尽管」，不是时间连词「当……时」。这是熟词僻义高频考点。"},{"en":"he has not been charged with the task of approaching","lit":"他并未被赋予……的任务","role":"（because 引导的原因从句的主句）","note":"难点： be charged with = 被赋予/被委以；被动化主动 be charged with sth. 在此处意为「被赋予……（职责/任务）」，不是「被指控」。汉语习惯主动表达，可译成「他并没有被赋予……的任务」或「他的任务并不是去……」。approaching 在此为「处理 / 探讨 / 着手解决」，不是「接近」。"},{"en":"any but the factual aspects of those problems.","lit":"这些问题的除事实层面之外的任何方面","role":"（approaching 的宾语（含 any but 限定））","note":"难点： any but = 除……之外的任何（含蓄否定） any but X 的字面是「除 X 之外的任何」，与前面的 not 配合等价于 only X——即「只去处理这些问题的事实方面」。这是本句最大的陷阱，主体考生容易漏掉 but 或者把 any but 翻反。those problems 回指 moral problems。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"But his primary task is not to think about the moral code which governs his activity, any more than a businessman is expected to dedicate his energies to an exploration of rules of conduct in business.","refZh":"但科学家的首要任务，并不是去思考约束自身活动的那套道德准则；正如人们也并不指望商人会把精力投入到对商业行为准则的探究中去一样。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"But his primary task is not to think about the moral code","lit":"但他的首要任务并不是去思考道德准则","role":"（主干：主系表（不定式作表语））","note":"难点： his = 普通科学家的（承前指代） his 仍然回指上一句的 the average scientist。翻译时第一次出现可显化为「科学家的」，后文承接即可。moral code 与全篇术语一致译「道德准则」。"},{"en":"which governs his activity,","lit":"约束/支配他活动的","role":"（限定 moral code 的 which 定语从句）","note":"难点： govern 此处不是「统治」而是「约束/支配」 govern 修饰 moral code 时取「约束、规范、支配」之义，搭配抽象主语（道德准则）+ 抽象宾语（行为/活动）。译「统治」会过重。短从句直接前置成「……的道德准则」。"},{"en":"any more than a businessman is expected to dedicate his energies to an exploration of rules of conduct in business.","lit":"正如商人也不被期望把精力投入到对商业行为准则的探究中一样","role":"（比较状语从句（A is not X any more than B is X））","note":"难点： not…any more than… = 与……一样不…… 这是本句最核心的采分点。A is not P any more than B is Q 的标准译法是「A 不 P，正如 B 也不 Q 一样」——两端都为否定。许多考生会错译成「比……更不」。配合后面的被动 is expected to（被期望/被要求）一并转主动：「商人不会被要求……」或「人们并不指望商人……」。rules of conduct 译「行为准则」，与前文的 moral code 形成对应。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"They may teach very well, and more than earn their salaries, but most of them make little or no independent reflections on human problems which involve moral judgment.","refZh":"这些教师或许教得很好，对得起自己的薪水甚至还绰绰有余；但他们当中大多数人对那些涉及道德判断的人类问题，很少进行独立思考，甚至根本不去思考。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"They may teach very well, and more than earn their salaries,","lit":"他们可能教得非常好，并且不仅仅是挣得他们的薪水","role":"（主干前半：并列两动作）","note":"难点： They = 教师们；more than earn their salaries = 不只是配得上自己的薪水 They 回指上一句 The definition also excludes the majority of teachers 中的 teachers，译文首次出现显化为「这些教师」。more than + 动词原形是固定结构，意为「远不止于、不仅仅、绰绰有余地」，更地道的中文是「对得起这份薪水还绰绰有余」或「完全配得上自己的薪水」，不是字面「挣得比薪水多」。"},{"en":"but most of them make little or no independent reflections on human problems","lit":"但他们大多数人对人类问题几乎没有或完全没有独立的思考","role":"（but 引导的转折分句的主干）","note":"难点： little or no = 几乎没有或根本没有（含蓄否定） little 本身已含否定意味（「几乎没有」），little or no 进一步强化为「几乎没有甚至根本没有」。reflections on 是固定搭配「对……的思考/反思」，independent 修饰它，强调「自己独立去想」——这正是作者定义「知识分子」的核心。"},{"en":"which involve moral judgment.","lit":"涉及道德判断的","role":"（限定 human problems 的 which 定语从句）","note":"难点： involve 取「涉及/牵涉」义；短从句前置 involve 在此不是「使卷入」，而是「涉及到、牵涉到」。短定语从句直接前置成「涉及道德判断的人类问题」。moral judgment 与全篇术语一致译「道德判断」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: You want to contribute to Project Hope by offering financial aid to a child in a remote area. Write a letter to the department concerned, asking them to help find a candidate. You should specify what kind of child you want to help and how you will carry out your plan. Write your letter in no less than 100 words. Write it neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: You want to contribute to Project Hope by offering financial aid to a child in a remote area. Write a letter to the department concerned, asking them to help find a candidate. You should specify what kind of child you want to help and how you will carry out your plan. Write your letter in no less than 100 words. Write it neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to seek your assistance in finding a child whom I would like to sponsor through Project Hope. As a beneficiary of education myself, I am eager to offer financial aid to a young learner in a remote area. The child I hope to support should come from a poor family that cannot afford the cost of schooling, preferably from a mountainous or underdeveloped region. Above all, he or she should be diligent, do well in study and have a genuine desire to continue learning, so that my help can truly change a life. As for my plan, I intend to send a fixed sum of money to the child at the beginning of every term to cover tuition and books. I will keep this support going until he or she finishes school, and I would also like to write letters regularly to follow the child's progress and offer encouragement. I would be very grateful if you could help me find a suitable candidate. I look forward to your reply. Yours faithfully, Li Ming","translation":"尊敬的先生或女士： 我写信是想请您协助我物色一名孩子，我希望通过希望工程资助他/她。我自己也曾受惠于教育，因此十分渴望为一名偏远地区的小学子提供经济上的帮助。 我希望资助的孩子应来自无力承担上学费用的贫困家庭，最好身处山区或欠发达地区。尤为重要的是，他或她应勤奋刻苦、学习成绩优良，并有继续求学的强烈愿望，这样我的帮助才能真正改变一个人的命运。 至于我的计划，我打算每学期开学时给这个孩子汇一笔固定的钱，用于支付学费和书本费。我会一直资助到他/她毕业，还愿意定期写信跟进孩子的进步、给予鼓励。 如蒙相助为我找到合适的人选，我将不胜感激。期待您的回复。 此致 李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"开门见山亮意图","text":"【第 1 段】 开门见山亮意图 。首段用 I am writing to seek your assistance in... 直接点明来意，再以 As a beneficiary of education myself, I am eager to offer financial aid 补出身份与资助意愿，落实了『称呼＋说明写信意图』这一功能，正对应句架『亮明写信目的』。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"分层写清孩子条件","text":"【第 2 段】 分层写清孩子条件 。第二段从家境（come from a poor family that cannot afford the cost of schooling）、地域（a mountainous or underdeveloped region）到品质（diligent, do well in study and have a genuine desire to continue learning）逐层限定，用 Above all... so that... 递进强调，答足了『想资助什么样的孩子』。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"把计划写成可操作步骤","text":"【第 3 段】 把计划写成可操作步骤 。第三段用 As for my plan, I intend to send a fixed sum of money... at the beginning of every term 给出金额与频率，keep this support going until... finishes school 给期限，write letters regularly 给跟进，把 how 答实、不空泛。"},{"tag":"【第 4 段】","core":"致谢期待并规范落款","text":"【第 4 段】 致谢期待并规范落款 。结尾用 I would be very grateful if you could... 礼貌致谢，I look forward to your reply 期待回复，落款只写 Li Ming、未署真名、也未写地址，卡住全部格式硬约束。"}],"wordCount":180}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Study the following photos carefully and write an essay in which you should 1)describe the photos briefly, 2)interpret the social phenomenon reflected by them, and 3)give your point of view. You should write 160-200 words neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Study the following photos carefully and write an essay in which you should 1)describe the photos briefly, 2)interpret the social phenomenon reflected by them, and 3)give your point of view. You should write 160-200 words neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2006-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一张拼贴图片，包含了两张照片和一段文字说明：“注：Beckham（贝克汉姆）——英国足球明星","width":"581","height":"431","local":"assets/writing/2006-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"The two photos vividly reveal an interesting yet thought-provoking scene. In the left picture, a young man has the word \"Beckham\", the name of a famous English football star, tattooed on his face; in the right one, another youngster is paying 300 yuan to have his hair braided into the fashionable \"Beckham style\". What these images convey is far beyond the pictures themselves. They reflect the increasingly blind idol worship prevailing among a large number of Chinese teenagers. In order to show their admiration, some young people imitate celebrities in every possible way, spending money lavishly and even permanently changing their appearance. Such fanaticism largely stems from the overwhelming entertainment media and a lack of firm self-identity. As far as I am concerned, admiring a star is quite natural, but worshipping one blindly deserves our caution. Instead of copying idols' hairstyles or faces, young people ought to learn from the diligence and professionalism behind their success. Only in this way can idols truly become a positive driving force rather than a shackle.","translation":"这两张照片生动地呈现了一幕既有趣又发人深省的画面。左图中，一个年轻人把英国足球明星贝克汉姆的名字纹在了脸上；右图中，另一个年轻人正花 300 元把头发编成时髦的'小贝头'。\n这些画面所传达的远不止照片本身。它们折射出在大量中国青少年中日益盛行的盲目偶像崇拜。为了表达爱慕，一些年轻人千方百计地模仿明星，挥霍钱财，甚至永久改变自己的外貌。这种狂热在很大程度上源于铺天盖地的娱乐媒体，以及缺乏稳固的自我认同。\n在我看来，欣赏一位明星本无可厚非，但盲目崇拜则值得我们警惕。与其复制偶像的发型或长相，年轻人更应学习他们成功背后的勤奋与敬业。唯有如此，偶像才能真正成为一种正向的动力，而非一副枷锁。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"两三句客观速描","text":"【第 1 段】 两三句客观速描 。用总起句 'The two photos vividly reveal…' 起头，再以 'In the left picture… in the right one…' 左右分述，只写脸上纹名字、花 300 元做发型这些可见事实，三句收住，落实了 describe the photos briefly 的 briefly 要求，没有提前评判。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"过渡句缝合并给成因","text":"【第 2 段】 过渡句缝合并给成因 。开头 'What these images convey is far beyond the pictures themselves. They reflect…' 正是'由画面滑向现象'的过渡与释义，点出 blind idol worship；接着 'Such fanaticism largely stems from…' 给出媒体与自我认同两点成因，完成 interpret the social phenomenon reflected by them。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"标志语亮立场＋对比收尾","text":"【第 3 段】 标志语亮立场＋对比收尾 。'As far as I am concerned…but…' 明确亮出让步加转折的观点；'Instead of copying… ought to learn from…' 用对比给建议；末句 'Only in this way can…' 回扣主题收束，兑现 give your point of view。"}],"wordCount":172}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 A Indeed · 2 B cope · 3 D toward · 4 A raise · 5 D Not · 6 C range · 7 B Although · 8 C increasing · 9 A predicts · 10 A assist · 11 C Even · 12 B shelter · 13 D wandering · 14 C while · 15 C survival · 16 A around · 17 B comprehensive · 18 C As · 19 A puts · 20 D coordination \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 A · 23 C · 24 D · 25 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 A · 27 B · 28 C · 29 D · 30 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 C · 32 A · 33 C · 34 D · 35 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 D · 37 B · 38 D · 39 B · 40 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"选句填空（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 C · 42 A · 43 B · 44 F · 45 D \n（逐题解析见 选句填空（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
